window.IELTS_TOPIC={"topic":8,"en":"Archaeology & Ancient Civilisations","zh":"考古與古文明","items":[{"w":"archaeology","pos":"n.","def":"the study of the past by digging up old objects and places","cn":"考古學","s":"My cousin chose to study ________ at university, because she loves finding out how people lived thousands of years ago.","zh":"我表姊選擇在大學念考古學,因為她很喜歡探究幾千年前的人們如何生活。","part":"A","sec":"Archaeology & Excavation 考古與發掘","lab":"A1","t":"考古學"},{"w":"archaeologist","pos":"n.","def":"a person who studies the past by digging up old things","cn":"考古學家","s":"The ________ carefully lifted the old pot out of the ground, and she smiled because it was still in one piece.","zh":"那位考古學家小心地把古老的陶罐從地下取出,她笑了,因為它仍然完整無缺。","part":"A","sec":"Archaeology & Excavation 考古與發掘","lab":"A2","t":"考古學家"},{"w":"archaeological","pos":"adj.","def":"connected with the study of ancient remains","cn":"考古的","s":"Builders found an ________ site under the new car park, so the work stopped while experts studied the area.","zh":"工人在新停車場底下發現了一個考古遺址,所以工程在專家研究這個區域時暫停了。","part":"A","sec":"Archaeology & Excavation 考古與發掘","lab":"A3","t":"考古"},{"w":"excavate","pos":"v.","def":"to dig carefully to find buried objects","cn":"發掘;挖掘","s":"The team plans to ________ the hill next summer, because local farmers have found old coins there for years.","zh":"團隊計畫明年夏天發掘這座山丘,因為當地農夫多年來一直在那裡發現古錢幣。","part":"A","sec":"Archaeology & Excavation 考古與發掘","lab":"A4","t":"發掘"},{"w":"excavation","pos":"n.","def":"the careful digging up of an old site","cn":"發掘(工作);挖掘","s":"The ________ lasted three months, and students from five countries helped the experts remove the soil by hand.","zh":"這次發掘工作持續了三個月,來自五個國家的學生協助專家們用手清除泥土。","part":"A","sec":"Archaeology & Excavation 考古與發掘","lab":"A5","t":"發掘工作"},{"w":"dig","pos":"n.","def":"an organised archaeological excavation","cn":"考古挖掘(活動)","s":"I joined a summer ________ in Greece last year, and I spent every morning brushing dirt off broken pottery.","zh":"我去年參加了希臘的一個夏季考古挖掘,每天早上都在刷掉碎陶片上的泥土。","part":"A","sec":"Archaeology & Excavation 考古與發掘","lab":"A6","t":"考古挖掘"},{"w":"trowel","pos":"n.","def":"a small hand tool with a flat blade for digging","cn":"小鏟子(考古用手鏟)","s":"Each volunteer was given a ________ and a bucket, and they started scraping the soil away very slowly.","zh":"每位志工都拿到一把小鏟子和一個水桶,然後他們開始非常緩慢地刮去泥土。","part":"A","sec":"Archaeology & Excavation 考古與發掘","lab":"A7","t":"小鏟子"},{"w":"sieve","pos":"n.","def":"a tool with a net that separates small things from soil","cn":"篩子","s":"We poured the soil through a ________, so even tiny beads and fish bones would not be thrown away.","zh":"我們把泥土倒進篩子裡,這樣連小珠子和魚骨頭都不會被丟掉。","part":"A","sec":"Archaeology & Excavation 考古與發掘","lab":"A8","t":"篩子"},{"w":"pit","pos":"n.","def":"a hole dug in the ground","cn":"坑;坑洞","s":"The workers found an ancient rubbish ________ full of broken bowls, and it told them a lot about what people ate.","zh":"工人們發現了一個裝滿破碗的古代垃圾坑,它透露了許多關於人們吃些什麼的資訊。","part":"A","sec":"Archaeology & Excavation 考古與發掘","lab":"A9","t":"坑"},{"w":"mound","pos":"n.","def":"a small hill made of earth or stones","cn":"土墩;土丘","s":"The grassy ________ near the village looked natural, but scientists discovered that it was actually an ancient grave.","zh":"村莊附近那座長滿草的土丘看起來像是天然的,但科學家發現它其實是一座古墓。","part":"A","sec":"Archaeology & Excavation 考古與發掘","lab":"A10","t":"土丘"},{"w":"stratum","pos":"n.","def":"one layer of soil or rock (plural: strata)","cn":"地層;層","s":"Each ________ of soil represents a different period, so the deepest objects are usually the oldest.","zh":"每一地層的土壤代表一個不同的時期,所以最深處的物品通常是最古老的。","part":"A","sec":"Archaeology & Excavation 考古與發掘","lab":"A11","t":"地層"},{"w":"unearth","pos":"v.","def":"to find something by digging it out of the ground","cn":"發掘出;出土","s":"Farmers often ________ old tools while ploughing their fields, and some of them are more than two thousand years old.","zh":"農夫在犁田時常常挖出古老的工具,其中一些已有兩千多年的歷史。","part":"A","sec":"Archaeology & Excavation 考古與發掘","lab":"A12","t":"挖出"},{"w":"ruin","pos":"n.","def":"the broken parts left of an old building","cn":"廢墟;遺跡","s":"We walked around the ________ of an old castle, and our guide explained how the walls had once looked.","zh":"我們在一座古城堡的廢墟周圍散步,導遊解釋了那些城牆以前的樣子。","part":"A","sec":"Archaeology & Excavation 考古與發掘","lab":"A13","t":"廢墟"},{"w":"remains","pos":"n.","def":"parts of something that are left after a long time","cn":"遺骸;遺跡","s":"The ________ of a Roman house were found under the shopping centre, so the builders had to change their plans.","zh":"在購物中心底下發現了羅馬房屋的遺跡,所以建商必須改變他們的計畫。","part":"A","sec":"Archaeology & Excavation 考古與發掘","lab":"A14","t":"遺跡"},{"w":"rubble","pos":"n.","def":"broken stones and bricks from a fallen building","cn":"瓦礫;碎石","s":"After the earthquake, the old temple was just a pile of ________, but archaeologists still found statues inside it.","zh":"地震過後,那座古老的寺廟只剩一堆瓦礫,但考古學家仍然在裡面找到雕像。","part":"A","sec":"Archaeology & Excavation 考古與發掘","lab":"A15","t":"瓦礫"},{"w":"buried","pos":"adj.","def":"hidden under the ground","cn":"被埋藏的","s":"The children dreamed of finding ________ treasure on the beach, but they only found an old bottle cap.","zh":"孩子們夢想在海灘上找到被埋藏的寶藏,但他們只找到一個舊瓶蓋。","part":"A","sec":"Archaeology & Excavation 考古與發掘","lab":"A16","t":"被埋藏的"},{"w":"brush","pos":"v.","def":"to clean something gently with a brush","cn":"刷;輕刷","s":"The students had to ________ the dirt away very gently, because the old bones could break easily.","zh":"學生們必須非常輕柔地刷掉泥土,因為那些古老的骨頭很容易斷裂。","part":"A","sec":"Archaeology & Excavation 考古與發掘","lab":"A17","t":"刷"},{"w":"fragment","pos":"n.","def":"a small broken piece of something","cn":"碎片;片段","s":"They found a ________ of a painted wall, and experts used it to imagine the colours of the whole room.","zh":"他們找到了一塊彩繪牆壁的碎片,專家用它來想像整個房間的顏色。","part":"A","sec":"Archaeology & Excavation 考古與發掘","lab":"A18","t":"碎片"},{"w":"shard","pos":"n.","def":"a sharp broken piece of pottery or glass","cn":"(陶瓷或玻璃)碎片","s":"Thousands of pottery ________ were collected from the site, and volunteers spent months trying to fit them together.","zh":"從遺址收集了數千片陶器碎片,志工們花了好幾個月試著把它們拼湊起來。","part":"A","sec":"Archaeology & Excavation 考古與發掘","lab":"A19","t":"碎片"},{"w":"hoard","pos":"n.","def":"a hidden collection of valuable things","cn":"窖藏;藏寶","s":"A man with a shovel discovered a ________ of silver coins in his garden, and the local museum bought it for a large sum.","zh":"一名拿著鏟子的男子在他的花園裡發現了一批銀幣窖藏,當地博物館以一大筆錢買下了它。","part":"A","sec":"Archaeology & Excavation 考古與發掘","lab":"A20","t":"批 窖藏"},{"w":"treasure","pos":"n.","def":"a collection of gold, jewels or valuable objects","cn":"寶藏;財寶","s":"The pirates in the story hid their ________ on an island, but nobody has ever found it.","zh":"故事中的海盜把他們的寶藏藏在一座島上,但從來沒有人找到過。","part":"A","sec":"Archaeology & Excavation 考古與發掘","lab":"A21","t":"寶藏"},{"w":"relic","pos":"n.","def":"an object that survives from the distant past","cn":"遺物;古物","s":"This old sword is a ________ from a battle that happened eight hundred years ago, so the museum keeps it behind glass.","zh":"這把古劍是八百年前一場戰役的遺物,所以博物館把它放在玻璃後面保存。","part":"A","sec":"Archaeology & Excavation 考古與發掘","lab":"A22","t":"遺物"},{"w":"antiquity","pos":"n.","def":"the ancient past, especially before the Middle Ages","cn":"古代;上古","s":"The city has been an important trading centre since ________, and you can still see Greek columns in the old town.","zh":"這座城市自古代以來就是重要的貿易中心,在舊城區裡仍然可以看到希臘式柱子。","part":"A","sec":"Archaeology & Excavation 考古與發掘","lab":"A23","t":"古代"},{"w":"loot","pos":"v.","def":"to steal things, especially from ancient sites","cn":"盜掘;劫掠","s":"Thieves came at night to ________ the tombs, so the government sent guards to protect the site.","zh":"小偷在夜裡來盜掘墳墓,所以政府派了警衛來保護遺址。","part":"A","sec":"Archaeology & Excavation 考古與發掘","lab":"A24","t":"盜掘"},{"w":"curator","pos":"n.","def":"a person in charge of a museum collection","cn":"(博物館)館長;策展人","s":"The ________ explained the history of each object, and the students took notes for their school project.","zh":"策展人解說了每件物品的歷史,學生們為他們的學校專題做筆記。","part":"A","sec":"Archaeology & Excavation 考古與發掘","lab":"A25","t":"策展人"},{"w":"catalogue","pos":"v.","def":"to make a detailed list of objects","cn":"編目;登錄","s":"After each dig, the team must ________ every object, so other researchers can find the information later.","zh":"每次挖掘之後,團隊都必須把每件物品編目,這樣其他研究人員之後才能找到資料。","part":"A","sec":"Archaeology & Excavation 考古與發掘","lab":"A26","t":"編目"},{"w":"aerial","pos":"adj.","def":"taken from or happening in the air","cn":"空中的;航空的","s":"________ photos taken by a drone showed the outline of an old village, although nothing was visible from the ground.","zh":"無人機拍攝的空中照片顯示出一座古老村莊的輪廓,雖然從地面上什麼也看不到。","part":"A","sec":"Archaeology & Excavation 考古與發掘","lab":"A27","t":"空中"},{"w":"ground-penetrating radar","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a machine that uses radio waves to see under the ground","cn":"透地雷達","s":"The team used ________ ________ to look under the field, so they knew where to dig before touching the soil.","zh":"團隊使用透地雷達探查田地底下,所以他們在動土之前就知道該在哪裡挖。","part":"A","sec":"Archaeology & Excavation 考古與發掘","lab":"A28","t":"透地雷達"},{"w":"topsoil","pos":"n.","def":"the top layer of soil","cn":"表土","s":"The workers removed the ________ with a small machine, and then they continued digging slowly by hand.","zh":"工人們用小型機器移除了表土,然後繼續用手慢慢挖掘。","part":"A","sec":"Archaeology & Excavation 考古與發掘","lab":"A29","t":"表土"},{"w":"waterlogged","pos":"adj.","def":"completely full of water","cn":"浸水的;水浸的","s":"Wood usually rots quickly, but in ________ ground it can survive for thousands of years because there is no air.","zh":"木頭通常很快就會腐爛,但在浸水的土地中它能保存數千年,因為那裡沒有空氣。","part":"A","sec":"Archaeology & Excavation 考古與發掘","lab":"A30","t":"浸水的"},{"w":"artefact","pos":"n.","def":"an object made by people long ago","cn":"文物;手工藝品","s":"Every ________ in the museum has a label, so visitors can learn where it was found and how old it is.","zh":"博物館裡的每件文物都有標籤,所以參觀者能知道它是在哪裡被發現以及有多古老。","part":"A","sec":"Artefacts & Materials 文物與材料","lab":"A31","t":"文物"},{"w":"pottery","pos":"n.","def":"pots and dishes made from baked clay","cn":"陶器","s":"Ancient ________ can tell us what people cooked, because scientists can test the food left inside the pots.","zh":"古代陶器能告訴我們人們煮了什麼,因為科學家可以檢驗殘留在罐子裡的食物。","part":"A","sec":"Artefacts & Materials 文物與材料","lab":"A32","t":"陶器"},{"w":"ceramic","pos":"adj.","def":"made of clay that has been baked hard","cn":"陶瓷的","s":"My grandmother collects old ________ bowls, and she keeps the most valuable one in a glass cabinet.","zh":"我奶奶收藏古老的陶瓷碗,她把最珍貴的那一個放在玻璃櫃裡。","part":"A","sec":"Artefacts & Materials 文物與材料","lab":"A33","t":"陶瓷"},{"w":"clay","pos":"n.","def":"soft, wet earth used to make pots","cn":"黏土","s":"The children shaped little animals out of ________, and their teacher baked them in the school oven.","zh":"孩子們用黏土捏出小動物,老師用學校的烤爐把它們烤硬。","part":"A","sec":"Artefacts & Materials 文物與材料","lab":"A34","t":"黏土"},{"w":"kiln","pos":"n.","def":"a very hot oven for baking pottery or bricks","cn":"窯","s":"Archaeologists found an ancient ________ near the river, so they believe the village made its own pots and bricks.","zh":"考古學家在河邊發現了一座古窯,所以他們相信這個村莊自己製作陶罐和磚塊。","part":"A","sec":"Artefacts & Materials 文物與材料","lab":"A35","t":"窯"},{"w":"urn","pos":"n.","def":"a large decorated pot, often used to hold ashes","cn":"甕;骨灰罈","s":"The beautiful ________ was found in a grave, and it still contained the ashes of a person who died long ago.","zh":"這個美麗的甕是在墳墓裡發現的,裡面仍然裝著一位很久以前去世之人的骨灰。","part":"A","sec":"Artefacts & Materials 文物與材料","lab":"A36","t":"甕"},{"w":"bead","pos":"n.","def":"a small ball with a hole, used to make jewellery","cn":"珠子","s":"The necklace was made from hundreds of glass ________, and each one was coloured by hand.","zh":"這條項鍊由數百顆玻璃珠子製成,每一顆都是手工上色的。","part":"A","sec":"Artefacts & Materials 文物與材料","lab":"A37","t":"珠子"},{"w":"ornament","pos":"n.","def":"an object used for decoration","cn":"裝飾品","s":"The rich family decorated their home with gold ________, but poor families used simple wooden ones.","zh":"富有的家庭用金色的裝飾品裝飾家裡,而貧窮的家庭則使用簡單的木製裝飾。","part":"A","sec":"Artefacts & Materials 文物與材料","lab":"A38","t":"裝飾品"},{"w":"figurine","pos":"n.","def":"a small statue of a person or animal","cn":"小雕像","s":"The tiny ________ of a horse is only five centimetres tall, but it is more than three thousand years old.","zh":"這尊馬的小雕像只有五公分高,但它已有三千多年的歷史。","part":"A","sec":"Artefacts & Materials 文物與材料","lab":"A39","t":"雕像"},{"w":"statue","pos":"n.","def":"a large figure of a person or animal made of stone or metal","cn":"雕像","s":"The ________ of the king stood in the city square for centuries, until an earthquake knocked it over.","zh":"國王的雕像在城市廣場上矗立了好幾個世紀,直到一場地震把它震倒了。","part":"A","sec":"Artefacts & Materials 文物與材料","lab":"A40","t":"雕像"},{"w":"carving","pos":"n.","def":"a shape or pattern cut into wood or stone","cn":"雕刻(品)","s":"The walls of the cave are covered with ________ of animals, and nobody knows exactly who made them.","zh":"洞穴的牆上布滿了動物的雕刻,沒有人確切知道是誰刻的。","part":"A","sec":"Artefacts & Materials 文物與材料","lab":"A41","t":"雕刻"},{"w":"engrave","pos":"v.","def":"to cut words or pictures into a hard surface","cn":"雕刻;刻上","s":"The workers used to ________ the king's name on every stone, so his power would be remembered forever.","zh":"工人們過去會在每塊石頭上刻上國王的名字,這樣他的權力就會永遠被記住。","part":"A","sec":"Artefacts & Materials 文物與材料","lab":"A42","t":"刻上"},{"w":"inscription","pos":"n.","def":"words cut into stone or metal","cn":"銘文;碑文","s":"The ________ on the gravestone was hard to read, but the expert slowly worked out the name of the woman.","zh":"墓碑上的銘文很難辨讀,但專家慢慢地解讀出了那名女子的名字。","part":"A","sec":"Artefacts & Materials 文物與材料","lab":"A43","t":"銘文"},{"w":"papyrus","pos":"n.","def":"paper made from a water plant by ancient Egyptians","cn":"莎草紙","s":"Ancient Egyptians wrote on ________ made from river plants, and some of these documents still survive today.","zh":"古埃及人在用河邊植物製成的莎草紙上書寫,其中一些文件至今仍然留存。","part":"A","sec":"Artefacts & Materials 文物與材料","lab":"A44","t":"莎草紙"},{"w":"parchment","pos":"n.","def":"writing material made from animal skin","cn":"羊皮紙","s":"Monks copied books by hand on ________, so a single book could take a whole year to finish.","zh":"修道士用手在羊皮紙上抄寫書籍,所以一本書可能要花整整一年才能完成。","part":"A","sec":"Artefacts & Materials 文物與材料","lab":"A45","t":"羊皮紙"},{"w":"manuscript","pos":"n.","def":"a book or document written by hand","cn":"手抄本;手稿","s":"The old ________ is kept in a dark room, because strong light could damage the ink on its pages.","zh":"這份古老的手抄本被保存在一間暗室裡,因為強光可能會損壞書頁上的墨水。","part":"A","sec":"Artefacts & Materials 文物與材料","lab":"A46","t":"手抄本"},{"w":"bronze","pos":"n.","def":"a hard brown metal made from copper and tin","cn":"青銅","s":"The soldiers carried weapons made of ________, and these were much stronger than the stone tools used before.","zh":"士兵們攜帶青銅製的武器,這些武器比之前使用的石器堅固得多。","part":"A","sec":"Artefacts & Materials 文物與材料","lab":"A47","t":"青銅"},{"w":"copper","pos":"n.","def":"a soft reddish-brown metal","cn":"銅","s":"People first learned to melt ________ about seven thousand years ago, and this changed how they made tools.","zh":"人類大約在七千年前首次學會熔化銅,這改變了他們製作工具的方式。","part":"A","sec":"Artefacts & Materials 文物與材料","lab":"A48","t":"銅"},{"w":"flint","pos":"n.","def":"a hard grey stone that breaks into sharp pieces","cn":"燧石;打火石","s":"Early humans made knives from ________, because the stone could be shaped into a very sharp edge.","zh":"早期人類用燧石製作刀子,因為這種石頭能被打製出非常鋒利的邊緣。","part":"A","sec":"Artefacts & Materials 文物與材料","lab":"A49","t":"燧石"},{"w":"obsidian","pos":"n.","def":"black glass formed from volcanic rock","cn":"黑曜石","s":"Tools made of ________ were traded over long distances, so scientists can trace ancient trade routes by studying them.","zh":"黑曜石製的工具被交易到很遠的地方,所以科學家能透過研究它們來追溯古代的貿易路線。","part":"A","sec":"Artefacts & Materials 文物與材料","lab":"A50","t":"黑曜石"},{"w":"antler","pos":"n.","def":"a branch-like horn on the head of a deer","cn":"鹿角","s":"Prehistoric people made needles and combs from deer ________, and some of them were beautifully decorated.","zh":"史前人類用鹿角製作針和梳子,其中一些裝飾得很精美。","part":"A","sec":"Artefacts & Materials 文物與材料","lab":"A51","t":"角"},{"w":"textile","pos":"n.","def":"cloth or woven material","cn":"紡織品;布料","s":"Ancient ________ rarely survive because cloth rots easily, but dry deserts have kept some pieces in good condition.","zh":"古代紡織品很少能保存下來,因為布料容易腐爛,但乾燥的沙漠讓一些布片保持在良好狀態。","part":"A","sec":"Artefacts & Materials 文物與材料","lab":"A52","t":"紡織品"},{"w":"loom","pos":"n.","def":"a machine or frame for weaving cloth","cn":"織布機","s":"The women in the village worked at a wooden ________ every evening, and they made beautiful cloth for the market.","zh":"村裡的婦女每天晚上都在木製織布機前工作,她們為市集織出美麗的布料。","part":"A","sec":"Artefacts & Materials 文物與材料","lab":"A53","t":"織布機"},{"w":"weave / wove / woven","pos":"v.","def":"to make cloth by crossing threads over and under","cn":"編織;織","s":"Thousands of years ago, people ________ baskets from grass, and some of these baskets were found in a dry cave.","zh":"幾千年前,人們用草編織籃子,其中一些籃子在一個乾燥的洞穴裡被發現。","part":"A","sec":"Artefacts & Materials 文物與材料","lab":"A54","t":"編織"},{"w":"dye","pos":"n.","def":"a substance used to change the colour of cloth","cn":"染料","s":"Purple ________ was very expensive in ancient times, so only kings and rich people could wear purple clothes.","zh":"紫色染料在古代非常昂貴,所以只有國王和富人才能穿紫色的衣服。","part":"A","sec":"Artefacts & Materials 文物與材料","lab":"A55","t":"染料"},{"w":"mosaic","pos":"n.","def":"a picture made from many small coloured stones","cn":"馬賽克;鑲嵌畫","s":"The floor of the Roman villa had a ________ of dolphins, and it still looked bright after two thousand years.","zh":"這座羅馬別墅的地板上有一幅海豚的鑲嵌畫,兩千年後它看起來仍然很鮮豔。","part":"A","sec":"Artefacts & Materials 文物與材料","lab":"A56","t":"鑲嵌畫"},{"w":"fresco","pos":"n.","def":"a painting made on wet plaster on a wall","cn":"濕壁畫","s":"The ________ on the church wall shows a famous story, but parts of it have faded because of damp air.","zh":"教堂牆上的濕壁畫描繪了一個著名的故事,但其中一些部分因為潮濕的空氣而褪色了。","part":"A","sec":"Artefacts & Materials 文物與材料","lab":"A57","t":"濕壁畫"},{"w":"pigment","pos":"n.","def":"a natural powder used to make colour","cn":"顏料;色素","s":"Cave artists mixed red ________ from crushed rocks with animal fat, and they painted with their fingers.","zh":"洞穴藝術家把壓碎的岩石製成的紅色顏料和動物油脂混合,然後用手指作畫。","part":"A","sec":"Artefacts & Materials 文物與材料","lab":"A58","t":"顏料"},{"w":"amulet","pos":"n.","def":"a small object worn to protect against bad luck","cn":"護身符","s":"The child was buried with a small ________ around her neck, because her parents believed it would keep her safe.","zh":"那個孩子下葬時脖子上戴著一個小護身符,因為她的父母相信它能保佑她平安。","part":"A","sec":"Artefacts & Materials 文物與材料","lab":"A59","t":"護身符"},{"w":"smelt","pos":"v.","def":"to heat rock to get metal out of it","cn":"冶煉;熔煉","s":"Ancient workers learned to ________ iron in hot fires, and this allowed them to make stronger tools and weapons.","zh":"古代工人學會在高溫的火中冶煉鐵,這讓他們能製造更堅固的工具和武器。","part":"A","sec":"Artefacts & Materials 文物與材料","lab":"A60","t":"冶煉"},{"w":"radiocarbon dating","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a method of finding the age of old organic material","cn":"放射性碳定年法","s":"________ ________ showed that the wooden boat was four thousand years old, so it is one of the oldest in Europe.","zh":"放射性碳定年法顯示這艘木船已有四千年歷史,所以它是歐洲最古老的船之一。","part":"A","sec":"Dating & Scientific Methods 年代測定與科學方法","lab":"A61","t":"放射性碳定年法"},{"w":"isotope","pos":"n.","def":"a form of a chemical element with a different weight","cn":"同位素","s":"By testing the ________ in a person's teeth, scientists can tell where that person grew up, even thousands of years later.","zh":"透過檢測一個人牙齒中的同位素,科學家即使在數千年後也能知道那個人在哪裡長大。","part":"A","sec":"Dating & Scientific Methods 年代測定與科學方法","lab":"A62","t":"同位素"},{"w":"half-life","pos":"n.","def":"the time it takes for half of a substance to disappear","cn":"半衰期","s":"Carbon-14 has a ________ of about 5,730 years, so it is useful for dating objects that are not too old.","zh":"碳十四的半衰期大約是五千七百三十年,所以它適合用來測定不太古老的物品年代。","part":"A","sec":"Dating & Scientific Methods 年代測定與科學方法","lab":"A63","t":"半衰期"},{"w":"dendrochronology","pos":"n.","def":"dating wood by counting and comparing tree rings","cn":"樹輪年代學","s":"Using ________, the team counted the rings in the old beams, and they found that the house was built in 1450.","zh":"團隊運用樹輪年代學計算舊樑木的年輪,發現這棟房子建於1450年。","part":"A","sec":"Dating & Scientific Methods 年代測定與科學方法","lab":"A64","t":"樹輪年代學"},{"w":"DNA","pos":"n.","def":"the material in cells that carries genetic information","cn":"去氧核糖核酸;DNA","s":"Scientists took ________ from the ancient bones, and they discovered that the man was related to people living nearby today.","zh":"科學家從古代骨骸中提取了DNA,發現這名男子與今天住在附近的人有親屬關係。","part":"A","sec":"Dating & Scientific Methods 年代測定與科學方法","lab":"A65","t":"DNA"},{"w":"genome","pos":"n.","def":"all the genetic information of a living thing","cn":"基因組","s":"Researchers studied the ________ of an ancient wolf, so they could learn when dogs first became pets.","zh":"研究人員研究了一隻古代狼的基因組,以便了解狗最初是何時成為寵物的。","part":"A","sec":"Dating & Scientific Methods 年代測定與科學方法","lab":"A66","t":"基因組"},{"w":"ancestry","pos":"n.","def":"the people your family came from in the past","cn":"祖先;血統","s":"Many people now test their ________ with a simple kit, and some are surprised to find relatives in other countries.","zh":"現在許多人用簡單的套組檢測自己的血統,有些人驚訝地發現自己在其他國家有親戚。","part":"A","sec":"Dating & Scientific Methods 年代測定與科學方法","lab":"A67","t":"血統"},{"w":"lineage","pos":"n.","def":"a line of family descent from an ancestor","cn":"世系;血統","s":"The noble family could trace its ________ back to a famous king, so they were proud of their history.","zh":"這個貴族家庭能把他們的世系追溯到一位著名的國王,所以他們以自己的歷史為傲。","part":"A","sec":"Dating & Scientific Methods 年代測定與科學方法","lab":"A68","t":"世系"},{"w":"microscope","pos":"n.","def":"an instrument that makes tiny things look bigger","cn":"顯微鏡","s":"Under the ________, the scientist saw tiny pieces of wheat on the stone tool, so she knew it was used for grinding grain.","zh":"在顯微鏡下,科學家在石器上看到微小的小麥碎屑,所以她知道它是用來磨穀物的。","part":"A","sec":"Dating & Scientific Methods 年代測定與科學方法","lab":"A69","t":"顯微鏡"},{"w":"residue","pos":"n.","def":"a small amount of something that remains after a process","cn":"殘留物;殘渣","s":"Scientists tested the ________ inside the old jar, and they found that it once held wine and honey.","zh":"科學家檢驗了古罐內的殘留物,發現它曾經裝過葡萄酒和蜂蜜。","part":"A","sec":"Dating & Scientific Methods 年代測定與科學方法","lab":"A70","t":"殘留物"},{"w":"pollen","pos":"n.","def":"fine powder from flowers","cn":"花粉","s":"Ancient ________ found in the mud showed which plants grew nearby, so experts could describe the landscape at that time.","zh":"在泥土中發現的古代花粉顯示附近生長過哪些植物,所以專家能描述當時的地景。","part":"A","sec":"Dating & Scientific Methods 年代測定與科學方法","lab":"A71","t":"花粉"},{"w":"timeline","pos":"n.","def":"a list of events in the order they happened","cn":"時間軸;年表","s":"Our teacher drew a ________ on the board, and we added the dates of each ancient empire in different colours.","zh":"老師在黑板上畫了一條時間軸,我們用不同顏色加上每個古代帝國的年代。","part":"A","sec":"Dating & Scientific Methods 年代測定與科學方法","lab":"A72","t":"時間軸"},{"w":"era","pos":"n.","def":"a long period of history","cn":"時代;紀元","s":"The Roman ________ brought new roads to Britain, and many of those roads are still used today.","zh":"羅馬時代為英國帶來了新的道路,其中許多道路至今仍在使用。","part":"A","sec":"Dating & Scientific Methods 年代測定與科學方法","lab":"A73","t":"時代"},{"w":"epoch","pos":"n.","def":"a period of time marked by special events","cn":"時期;紀元","s":"The invention of writing began a new ________ in human history, because knowledge could finally be recorded.","zh":"文字的發明開啟了人類歷史的新紀元,因為知識終於可以被記錄下來。","part":"A","sec":"Dating & Scientific Methods 年代測定與科學方法","lab":"A74","t":"紀元"},{"w":"millennium","pos":"n.","def":"a period of one thousand years","cn":"一千年;千禧年","s":"The village has existed for more than a ________, and some of its families have lived there for forty generations.","zh":"這個村莊已經存在超過一千年,其中一些家族已經在那裡住了四十代。","part":"A","sec":"Dating & Scientific Methods 年代測定與科學方法","lab":"A75","t":"一千年"},{"w":"replica","pos":"n.","def":"an exact copy of an object","cn":"複製品","s":"The museum shows a ________ of the golden mask, because the real one is too valuable to put on display.","zh":"博物館展示的是黃金面具的複製品,因為真品太珍貴而無法公開展示。","part":"A","sec":"Dating & Scientific Methods 年代測定與科學方法","lab":"A76","t":"複製品"},{"w":"reconstruct","pos":"v.","def":"to build or create something again from pieces of evidence","cn":"重建;重現","s":"Artists used the skull to ________ the woman's face, and visitors could finally see what she might have looked like.","zh":"藝術家利用頭骨重建了那名女子的臉孔,參觀者終於能看見她可能的樣貌。","part":"A","sec":"Dating & Scientific Methods 年代測定與科學方法","lab":"A77","t":"重建"},{"w":"forgery","pos":"n.","def":"a copy made to trick people into thinking it is real","cn":"贗品;偽造品","s":"The famous statue turned out to be a ________, because tests showed that the paint was only fifty years old.","zh":"那座著名的雕像原來是贗品,因為檢測顯示顏料只有五十年的歷史。","part":"A","sec":"Dating & Scientific Methods 年代測定與科學方法","lab":"A78","t":"贗品"},{"w":"organic","pos":"adj.","def":"coming from living things such as plants or animals","cn":"有機的","s":"________ materials like wood and leather usually rot away, but they can survive in very dry or very cold places.","zh":"像木頭和皮革這樣的有機材料通常會腐爛,但它們能在非常乾燥或非常寒冷的地方保存下來。","part":"A","sec":"Dating & Scientific Methods 年代測定與科學方法","lab":"A79","t":"有機"},{"w":"decompose","pos":"v.","def":"to break down slowly after death","cn":"分解;腐爛","s":"Bodies usually ________ quickly in warm soil, but the man found in the ice was almost perfectly preserved.","zh":"屍體在溫暖的土壤中通常很快就會腐爛,但在冰中發現的那名男子幾乎被完整保存下來。","part":"A","sec":"Dating & Scientific Methods 年代測定與科學方法","lab":"A80","t":"腐爛"},{"w":"fossil","pos":"n.","def":"the remains of an ancient plant or animal in rock","cn":"化石","s":"My brother found a ________ of a small sea creature on the beach, although the beach is now far from the sea.","zh":"我弟弟在海灘上發現了一塊小型海洋生物的化石,雖然那片海灘現在離海很遠。","part":"A","sec":"Dating & Scientific Methods 年代測定與科學方法","lab":"A81","t":"化石"},{"w":"corrode","pos":"v.","def":"to be slowly damaged by water or chemicals","cn":"腐蝕;鏽蝕","s":"Iron objects ________ quickly in wet soil, so ancient swords are often found as lumps of rust.","zh":"鐵器在潮濕的土壤中很快就會腐蝕,所以古劍常常以一團鏽塊的樣子被發現。","part":"A","sec":"Dating & Scientific Methods 年代測定與科學方法","lab":"A82","t":"腐蝕"},{"w":"geologist","pos":"n.","def":"a scientist who studies rocks and the earth","cn":"地質學家","s":"A ________ helped the team understand the rock layers, so they could estimate when the river had flooded.","zh":"一位地質學家幫助團隊了解岩層,所以他們能估計河流氾濫的時間。","part":"A","sec":"Dating & Scientific Methods 年代測定與科學方法","lab":"A83","t":"地質學家"},{"w":"X-ray","pos":"n.","def":"a picture that shows the inside of an object","cn":"X光(片)","s":"An ________ of the mummy showed a broken leg, so experts think the man may have died after an accident.","zh":"木乃伊的X光顯示一條斷腿,所以專家認為這名男子可能是在一場意外後去世的。","part":"A","sec":"Dating & Scientific Methods 年代測定與科學方法","lab":"A84","t":"X光"},{"w":"centuries-old","pos":"adj.","def":"having existed for hundreds of years","cn":"數百年歷史的","s":"The ________ bridge is still used by cars today, although it was built for horses and carts.","zh":"這座有數百年歷史的橋至今仍有汽車通行,雖然它當初是為馬和馬車而建的。","part":"A","sec":"Dating & Scientific Methods 年代測定與科學方法","lab":"A85","t":"有數百年歷史的"},{"w":"bacteria","pos":"n.","def":"very small living things that can cause decay","cn":"細菌","s":"In cold, dry places, ________ cannot grow easily, so ancient bodies and clothes are often well preserved.","zh":"在寒冷乾燥的地方細菌不容易生長,所以古代的遺體和衣物常常保存得很好。","part":"A","sec":"Dating & Scientific Methods 年代測定與科學方法","lab":"A86","t":"細菌"},{"w":"civilisation","pos":"n.","def":"a developed society with cities, laws and writing","cn":"文明","s":"The Maya built a great ________ in the rainforest, but many of their cities were empty by the year 900.","zh":"馬雅人在雨林中建立了一個偉大的文明,但到了西元900年,他們的許多城市都已空無一人。","part":"A","sec":"Ancient Civilisations & Societies 古文明與社會","lab":"A87","t":"文明"},{"w":"ancient","pos":"adj.","def":"very old; from a long time ago","cn":"古代的;古老的","s":"We visited an ________ temple in Cambodia, and our guide said it was built almost a thousand years ago.","zh":"我們參觀了柬埔寨的一座古老寺廟,導遊說它幾乎是一千年前建造的。","part":"A","sec":"Ancient Civilisations & Societies 古文明與社會","lab":"A88","t":"古老"},{"w":"empire","pos":"n.","def":"a group of countries ruled by one powerful ruler","cn":"帝國","s":"The Roman ________ once stretched from Britain to Egypt, so people in many lands used the same coins.","zh":"羅馬帝國曾經從不列顛延伸到埃及,所以許多地方的人使用相同的錢幣。","part":"A","sec":"Ancient Civilisations & Societies 古文明與社會","lab":"A89","t":"帝國"},{"w":"emperor","pos":"n.","def":"the male ruler of an empire","cn":"皇帝","s":"The first ________ of China connected many walls to protect his land, but thousands of workers died building them.","zh":"中國的第一位皇帝把許多城牆連接起來保護他的領土,但數千名工人在建造時喪生。","part":"A","sec":"Ancient Civilisations & Societies 古文明與社會","lab":"A90","t":"皇帝"},{"w":"dynasty","pos":"n.","def":"a series of rulers from the same family","cn":"王朝;朝代","s":"The Tang ________ was famous for poetry and trade, and many foreigners lived in its capital city.","zh":"唐朝以詩歌和貿易聞名,許多外國人居住在它的首都。","part":"A","sec":"Ancient Civilisations & Societies 古文明與社會","lab":"A91","t":"朝"},{"w":"pharaoh","pos":"n.","def":"a king of ancient Egypt","cn":"法老","s":"The young ________ died when he was only nineteen, but his tomb was filled with golden treasures.","zh":"那位年輕的法老年僅十九歲就去世了,但他的墳墓裡裝滿了黃金寶藏。","part":"A","sec":"Ancient Civilisations & Societies 古文明與社會","lab":"A92","t":"法老"},{"w":"monarch","pos":"n.","def":"a king or queen","cn":"君主","s":"The ________ lived in a huge palace, while most ordinary people lived in small houses made of mud.","zh":"君主住在一座巨大的宮殿裡,而大多數平民住在泥土做的小房子裡。","part":"A","sec":"Ancient Civilisations & Societies 古文明與社會","lab":"A93","t":"君主"},{"w":"kingdom","pos":"n.","def":"a country ruled by a king or queen","cn":"王國","s":"The small ________ grew rich from trade, so neighbouring rulers often tried to take control of it.","zh":"這個小王國因貿易而富裕,所以鄰近的統治者常常試圖控制它。","part":"A","sec":"Ancient Civilisations & Societies 古文明與社會","lab":"A94","t":"王國"},{"w":"reign","pos":"n.","def":"the period when a king or queen rules","cn":"統治期間;在位期","s":"During the queen's long ________, the country built many roads, and trade with other lands grew quickly.","zh":"在女王漫長的統治期間,國家修建了許多道路,與其他地區的貿易也迅速成長。","part":"A","sec":"Ancient Civilisations & Societies 古文明與社會","lab":"A95","t":"統治期間"},{"w":"city-state","pos":"n.","def":"a city that governs itself like an independent country","cn":"城邦","s":"Athens was a powerful ________ in ancient Greece, and it had its own army, laws and coins.","zh":"雅典是古希臘一個強大的城邦,它擁有自己的軍隊、法律和錢幣。","part":"A","sec":"Ancient Civilisations & Societies 古文明與社會","lab":"A96","t":"城邦"},{"w":"citizen","pos":"n.","def":"a person who belongs to a city or country and has rights","cn":"公民;市民","s":"In ancient Athens, every male ________ could vote, but women and foreigners were not allowed to take part.","zh":"在古雅典,每位男性公民都可以投票,但女性和外國人不被允許參與。","part":"A","sec":"Ancient Civilisations & Societies 古文明與社會","lab":"A97","t":"公民"},{"w":"democracy","pos":"n.","def":"a system where people choose their leaders by voting","cn":"民主(制度)","s":"The idea of ________ began in ancient Greece, although only a small group of people could actually vote.","zh":"民主的概念起源於古希臘,雖然實際上只有一小群人能投票。","part":"A","sec":"Ancient Civilisations & Societies 古文明與社會","lab":"A98","t":"民主"},{"w":"republic","pos":"n.","def":"a country with elected leaders and no king","cn":"共和國","s":"Rome was a ________ for nearly five hundred years, but later it was ruled by emperors.","zh":"羅馬作為共和國將近五百年,但後來由皇帝統治。","part":"A","sec":"Ancient Civilisations & Societies 古文明與社會","lab":"A99","t":"共和國"},{"w":"senate","pos":"n.","def":"a group of important people who make laws","cn":"元老院;參議院","s":"The Roman ________ met in a large building in the city centre, and its members argued about wars and taxes.","zh":"羅馬元老院在市中心的一棟大建築裡開會,議員們爭論戰爭和稅收的問題。","part":"A","sec":"Ancient Civilisations & Societies 古文明與社會","lab":"A100","t":"元老院"},{"w":"aristocrat","pos":"n.","def":"a person from a rich, noble family","cn":"貴族","s":"The ________ wore silk robes and gold rings, so everyone in the street knew he was an important man.","zh":"那位貴族穿著絲綢長袍和金戒指,所以街上的每個人都知道他是個重要人物。","part":"A","sec":"Ancient Civilisations & Societies 古文明與社會","lab":"A101","t":"貴族"},{"w":"peasant","pos":"n.","def":"a poor farmer in the past","cn":"農民;佃農","s":"A ________ worked in the fields from morning to night, but he had to give much of his harvest to the landowner.","zh":"一位農民從早到晚在田裡工作,但他必須把大部分收成交給地主。","part":"A","sec":"Ancient Civilisations & Societies 古文明與社會","lab":"A102","t":"農民"},{"w":"priest","pos":"n.","def":"a person who performs religious ceremonies","cn":"祭司;神職人員","s":"The ________ climbed to the top of the temple each morning, and he watched the sky to predict the weather.","zh":"祭司每天早上爬到神廟頂端,觀察天空來預測天氣。","part":"A","sec":"Ancient Civilisations & Societies 古文明與社會","lab":"A103","t":"祭司"},{"w":"deity","pos":"n.","def":"a god or goddess","cn":"神;神祇","s":"Each city in ancient Egypt had its own ________, and people built temples to ask for good harvests.","zh":"古埃及的每個城市都有自己的神祇,人們建造神廟來祈求豐收。","part":"A","sec":"Ancient Civilisations & Societies 古文明與社會","lab":"A104","t":"神祇"},{"w":"worship","pos":"v.","def":"to show respect and love to a god","cn":"崇拜;敬拜","s":"Ancient farmers used to ________ the sun, because they knew that their crops could not grow without it.","zh":"古代農民過去會崇拜太陽,因為他們知道沒有它作物就無法生長。","part":"A","sec":"Ancient Civilisations & Societies 古文明與社會","lab":"A105","t":"崇拜"},{"w":"ritual","pos":"n.","def":"a ceremony that is always done in the same way","cn":"儀式","s":"The ________ took place every spring, and the whole village danced and shared food to welcome the new season.","zh":"這個儀式每年春天舉行,全村的人一起跳舞並分享食物來迎接新的季節。","part":"A","sec":"Ancient Civilisations & Societies 古文明與社會","lab":"A106","t":"儀式"},{"w":"offering","pos":"n.","def":"a gift given to a god","cn":"祭品;供品","s":"People left food and flowers as an ________ at the temple, because they hoped the gods would protect their families.","zh":"人們把食物和花留在神廟作為供品,因為他們希望神明保佑他們的家人。","part":"A","sec":"Ancient Civilisations & Societies 古文明與社會","lab":"A107","t":"供品"},{"w":"myth","pos":"n.","def":"an ancient story about gods and heroes","cn":"神話","s":"The Greek ________ about a hero who fights a monster is still popular, and many films have retold it.","zh":"那則關於英雄與怪物戰鬥的希臘神話至今仍很受歡迎,許多電影都重新講述過它。","part":"A","sec":"Ancient Civilisations & Societies 古文明與社會","lab":"A108","t":"神話"},{"w":"legend","pos":"n.","def":"an old story that may be partly true","cn":"傳說","s":"According to ________, a golden city lies hidden in the jungle, but explorers have never found it.","zh":"根據傳說,有一座黃金城市隱藏在叢林裡,但探險家們從未找到它。","part":"A","sec":"Ancient Civilisations & Societies 古文明與社會","lab":"A109","t":"傳說"},{"w":"scribe","pos":"n.","def":"a person whose job was to write documents in the past","cn":"抄寫員;書記","s":"Only a ________ could read and write in ancient Egypt, so these men were highly respected.","zh":"在古埃及只有書記會讀寫,所以這些人非常受尊敬。","part":"A","sec":"Ancient Civilisations & Societies 古文明與社會","lab":"A110","t":"書記"},{"w":"hieroglyphs","pos":"n.","def":"picture symbols used in ancient Egyptian writing","cn":"象形文字","s":"The walls of the tomb were covered with ________, and experts spent years learning what they meant.","zh":"墳墓的牆上布滿了象形文字,專家們花了好幾年才弄懂它們的意思。","part":"A","sec":"Ancient Civilisations & Societies 古文明與社會","lab":"A111","t":"象形文字"},{"w":"alphabet","pos":"n.","def":"a set of letters used to write a language","cn":"字母(表)","s":"The Phoenicians created an ________ with only twenty-two letters, so writing became much easier to learn.","zh":"腓尼基人創造了一套只有二十二個字母的字母表,所以書寫變得容易學習多了。","part":"A","sec":"Ancient Civilisations & Societies 古文明與社會","lab":"A112","t":"字母表"},{"w":"calendar","pos":"n.","def":"a system for dividing the year into days and months","cn":"曆法;日曆","s":"The Maya had a very accurate ________, because their priests studied the movements of the sun and the stars.","zh":"馬雅人有非常精確的曆法,因為他們的祭司研究太陽和星星的運行。","part":"A","sec":"Ancient Civilisations & Societies 古文明與社會","lab":"A113","t":"曆法"},{"w":"astronomy","pos":"n.","def":"the scientific study of stars and planets","cn":"天文學","s":"Ancient Babylonians were skilled in ________, and they could predict when the moon would turn dark.","zh":"古巴比倫人精通天文學,他們能預測月亮何時會變暗。","part":"A","sec":"Ancient Civilisations & Societies 古文明與社會","lab":"A114","t":"天文學"},{"w":"philosopher","pos":"n.","def":"a person who thinks deeply about life and truth","cn":"哲學家","s":"The Greek ________ taught his students by asking questions, and his method is still used in classrooms today.","zh":"那位希臘哲學家以提問的方式教導學生,而他的方法至今仍在教室中使用。","part":"A","sec":"Ancient Civilisations & Societies 古文明與社會","lab":"A115","t":"哲學家"},{"w":"tribute","pos":"n.","def":"payment given by a weaker ruler to a stronger one","cn":"貢品;進貢","s":"Small kingdoms had to send ________ to the emperor every year, so his palace was full of gold and silk.","zh":"小王國每年都必須向皇帝送上貢品,所以他的宮殿裡堆滿了黃金和絲綢。","part":"A","sec":"Ancient Civilisations & Societies 古文明與社會","lab":"A116","t":"貢品"},{"w":"monument","pos":"n.","def":"a building or statue built to remember a person or event","cn":"紀念碑;古蹟","s":"Stonehenge is a famous ________ in England, and thousands of visitors come to see the sunrise there in summer.","zh":"巨石陣是英國一座著名的古蹟,夏天有數千名遊客來這裡看日出。","part":"A","sec":"Monuments, Architecture & Burial 古蹟、建築與墓葬","lab":"A117","t":"古蹟"},{"w":"megalith","pos":"n.","def":"a very large stone used in ancient monuments","cn":"巨石","s":"Each ________ weighs about twenty-five tons, so nobody is sure how ancient people moved them so far.","zh":"每塊巨石重約二十五噸,所以沒有人確定古人是如何把它們搬運得那麼遠的。","part":"A","sec":"Monuments, Architecture & Burial 古蹟、建築與墓葬","lab":"A118","t":"巨石"},{"w":"pyramid","pos":"n.","def":"a huge stone building with four sloping sides","cn":"金字塔","s":"The Great ________ took about twenty years to build, and it was the tallest building in the world for centuries.","zh":"大金字塔花了大約二十年建造,並在好幾個世紀裡都是世界上最高的建築。","part":"A","sec":"Monuments, Architecture & Burial 古蹟、建築與墓葬","lab":"A119","t":"金字塔"},{"w":"temple","pos":"n.","def":"a building used for religious worship","cn":"神廟;寺廟","s":"The ________ stood on top of a hill, so the priests could see the whole valley from its steps.","zh":"那座神廟矗立在山頂上,所以祭司們能從它的台階上看到整個山谷。","part":"A","sec":"Monuments, Architecture & Burial 古蹟、建築與墓葬","lab":"A120","t":"神廟"},{"w":"palace","pos":"n.","def":"a large, grand house of a king or queen","cn":"宮殿","s":"The king's ________ had more than a thousand rooms, and some of them had beautiful paintings on the walls.","zh":"國王的宮殿有一千多個房間,其中一些房間的牆上有美麗的壁畫。","part":"A","sec":"Monuments, Architecture & Burial 古蹟、建築與墓葬","lab":"A121","t":"宮殿"},{"w":"citadel","pos":"n.","def":"a strong fortress on high ground in or near a city","cn":"城堡;要塞","s":"The people ran to the ________ when the enemy arrived, because its thick walls could protect them.","zh":"敵人來襲時,人們跑進要塞,因為它厚厚的城牆能保護他們。","part":"A","sec":"Monuments, Architecture & Burial 古蹟、建築與墓葬","lab":"A122","t":"要塞"},{"w":"rampart","pos":"n.","def":"a wide wall of earth or stone built for defence","cn":"城牆;壁壘","s":"The old town is surrounded by a stone ________, and today tourists can walk along the top of it.","zh":"舊城區被一道石砌城牆環繞,今天遊客可以沿著城牆頂端散步。","part":"A","sec":"Monuments, Architecture & Burial 古蹟、建築與墓葬","lab":"A123","t":"城牆"},{"w":"amphitheatre","pos":"n.","def":"a round open building with rows of seats","cn":"圓形劇場","s":"The Roman ________ could hold fifty thousand people, and they came to watch shows and contests.","zh":"羅馬圓形劇場能容納五萬人,他們來這裡觀看表演和比賽。","part":"A","sec":"Monuments, Architecture & Burial 古蹟、建築與墓葬","lab":"A124","t":"圓形劇場"},{"w":"aqueduct","pos":"n.","def":"a bridge-like structure that carries water","cn":"導水渠;高架渠","s":"The Romans built a long ________ to bring fresh water into the city, and part of it still stands today.","zh":"羅馬人建造了一條很長的導水渠把淡水引進城市,其中一部分至今仍然屹立。","part":"A","sec":"Monuments, Architecture & Burial 古蹟、建築與墓葬","lab":"A125","t":"導水渠"},{"w":"pillar","pos":"n.","def":"a tall column that supports a roof","cn":"柱子","s":"Each ________ in the temple is carved with flowers, and together they hold up the heavy stone roof.","zh":"神廟裡的每根柱子都刻有花朵,它們一起支撐著沉重的石製屋頂。","part":"A","sec":"Monuments, Architecture & Burial 古蹟、建築與墓葬","lab":"A126","t":"柱子"},{"w":"arch","pos":"n.","def":"a curved structure over an opening","cn":"拱門;拱形結構","s":"The Romans used the ________ to build strong bridges, because the curved shape spreads the weight evenly.","zh":"羅馬人使用拱形結構建造堅固的橋樑,因為弧形能平均分散重量。","part":"A","sec":"Monuments, Architecture & Burial 古蹟、建築與墓葬","lab":"A127","t":"拱形結構"},{"w":"dome","pos":"n.","def":"a round roof shaped like half a ball","cn":"圓頂","s":"The huge ________ of the building was the largest in the world for many years, and it still has no cracks.","zh":"這棟建築巨大的圓頂多年來是世界上最大的,而且至今仍沒有裂縫。","part":"A","sec":"Monuments, Architecture & Burial 古蹟、建築與墓葬","lab":"A128","t":"圓頂"},{"w":"masonry","pos":"n.","def":"the stones or bricks that make up a building","cn":"石造結構;磚石","s":"The ________ of the old castle was so well made that the stones fit together without any cement.","zh":"這座古城堡的石造結構做得非常好,石塊之間不用任何水泥就能緊密接合。","part":"A","sec":"Monuments, Architecture & Burial 古蹟、建築與墓葬","lab":"A129","t":"石造結構"},{"w":"quarry","pos":"n.","def":"a place where stone is dug out of the ground","cn":"採石場","s":"The stones for the temple came from a ________ twenty kilometres away, so workers had to drag them across the hills.","zh":"建造神廟的石頭來自二十公里外的採石場,所以工人必須把它們拖過山丘。","part":"A","sec":"Monuments, Architecture & Burial 古蹟、建築與墓葬","lab":"A130","t":"採石場"},{"w":"boulder","pos":"n.","def":"a very large rock","cn":"巨石;大圓石","s":"A huge ________ blocked the entrance to the cave, and it took ten men to roll it away.","zh":"一塊巨大的大圓石擋住了洞穴的入口,需要十個人才能把它滾開。","part":"A","sec":"Monuments, Architecture & Burial 古蹟、建築與墓葬","lab":"A131","t":"大圓石"},{"w":"slab","pos":"n.","def":"a thick, flat piece of stone","cn":"石板;厚板","s":"The tomb was covered by a heavy stone ________, so robbers could not open it easily.","zh":"墳墓被一塊沉重的石板蓋住,所以盜墓者無法輕易打開它。","part":"A","sec":"Monuments, Architecture & Burial 古蹟、建築與墓葬","lab":"A132","t":"石板"},{"w":"brick","pos":"n.","def":"a block of baked clay used for building","cn":"磚塊","s":"The ancient city was built with mud ________, and the workers dried them in the hot sun before using them.","zh":"這座古城是用泥磚建造的,工人們在使用前先把磚塊放在烈日下曬乾。","part":"A","sec":"Monuments, Architecture & Burial 古蹟、建築與墓葬","lab":"A133","t":"磚"},{"w":"mortar","pos":"n.","def":"a mixture used to hold bricks or stones together","cn":"灰漿;砂漿","s":"Roman ________ was so strong that some of their walls are still standing after two thousand years.","zh":"羅馬的灰漿非常堅固,所以他們的一些城牆在兩千年後仍然屹立。","part":"A","sec":"Monuments, Architecture & Burial 古蹟、建築與墓葬","lab":"A134","t":"灰漿"},{"w":"tomb","pos":"n.","def":"a large grave, often with a building over it","cn":"墳墓;陵墓","s":"The ________ of the king was hidden deep under the mountain, so it stayed safe from robbers for centuries.","zh":"國王的陵墓深藏在山底下,所以好幾個世紀都沒有被盜墓者破壞。","part":"A","sec":"Monuments, Architecture & Burial 古蹟、建築與墓葬","lab":"A135","t":"陵墓"},{"w":"burial","pos":"n.","def":"the act of putting a dead body in the ground","cn":"埋葬;葬禮","s":"The way a society handled ________ tells us a lot, because it shows what people believed about death.","zh":"一個社會處理埋葬的方式告訴我們很多事,因為它顯示了人們對死亡的看法。","part":"A","sec":"Monuments, Architecture & Burial 古蹟、建築與墓葬","lab":"A136","t":"埋葬"},{"w":"grave","pos":"n.","def":"a place in the ground where a dead person is buried","cn":"墳墓","s":"Archaeologists found a ________ containing a warrior and his horse, and both were buried with gold jewellery.","zh":"考古學家發現了一座墳墓,裡面埋著一名戰士和他的馬,兩者都戴著金飾下葬。","part":"A","sec":"Monuments, Architecture & Burial 古蹟、建築與墓葬","lab":"A137","t":"墳墓"},{"w":"coffin","pos":"n.","def":"a box in which a dead body is buried","cn":"棺材","s":"The wooden ________ was painted with bright colours, and it still looked new when the team opened the tomb.","zh":"那具木棺材漆著鮮豔的顏色,團隊打開墳墓時它看起來仍然像新的。","part":"A","sec":"Monuments, Architecture & Burial 古蹟、建築與墓葬","lab":"A138","t":"棺材"},{"w":"sarcophagus","pos":"n.","def":"a stone coffin, often decorated","cn":"石棺","s":"The heavy ________ was carved with pictures of the dead man's life, and it took eight workers to lift its lid.","zh":"那具沉重的石棺刻有死者生平的圖案,需要八名工人才能抬起它的蓋子。","part":"A","sec":"Monuments, Architecture & Burial 古蹟、建築與墓葬","lab":"A139","t":"石棺"},{"w":"mummify","pos":"v.","def":"to preserve a dead body by drying and wrapping it","cn":"製成木乃伊","s":"Ancient Egyptians used salt to ________ their dead, because they believed the body was needed in the afterlife.","zh":"古埃及人用鹽把死者製成木乃伊,因為他們相信來世需要這具身體。","part":"A","sec":"Monuments, Architecture & Burial 古蹟、建築與墓葬","lab":"A140","t":"製成木乃伊"},{"w":"embalm","pos":"v.","def":"to treat a dead body with chemicals to stop it decaying","cn":"(用防腐劑)保存屍體","s":"Priests would ________ the body with oils and spices, and then they wrapped it in long strips of cloth.","zh":"祭司們會用油和香料為屍體防腐,然後用長條布把它包裹起來。","part":"A","sec":"Monuments, Architecture & Burial 古蹟、建築與墓葬","lab":"A141","t":"為屍體防腐"},{"w":"cemetery","pos":"n.","def":"a large area of land where people are buried","cn":"墓地;公墓","s":"The old ________ outside the town has graves from five hundred years ago, so historians often visit it.","zh":"鎮外那座古老的墓地有五百年前的墳墓,所以歷史學家常常去那裡參訪。","part":"A","sec":"Monuments, Architecture & Burial 古蹟、建築與墓葬","lab":"A142","t":"墓地"},{"w":"chamber","pos":"n.","def":"a room, especially one inside a tomb or palace","cn":"室;墓室","s":"The secret ________ inside the pyramid was discovered using special cameras, but nobody has entered it yet.","zh":"金字塔內的秘密墓室是用特殊攝影機發現的,但還沒有人進去過。","part":"A","sec":"Monuments, Architecture & Burial 古蹟、建築與墓葬","lab":"A143","t":"墓室"},{"w":"afterlife","pos":"n.","def":"a life that some people believe begins after death","cn":"來世","s":"People were buried with food and tools, because they believed they would need them in the ________.","zh":"人們下葬時會帶著食物和工具,因為他們相信在來世會需要這些東西。","part":"A","sec":"Monuments, Architecture & Burial 古蹟、建築與墓葬","lab":"A144","t":"來世"},{"w":"grave goods","pos":"n.phr.","def":"objects buried with a dead person","cn":"陪葬品","s":"The ________ ________ in the tomb included gold cups and weapons, so experts believe the woman was a powerful leader.","zh":"墳墓中的陪葬品包括金杯和武器,所以專家相信這名女子是一位有權勢的領袖。","part":"A","sec":"Monuments, Architecture & Burial 古蹟、建築與墓葬","lab":"A145","t":"陪葬品"},{"w":"solstice","pos":"n.","def":"the longest or shortest day of the year","cn":"至日(夏至或冬至)","s":"On the summer ________, the sun rises exactly between the two largest stones, and crowds gather to watch it.","zh":"在夏至那天,太陽正好從兩塊最大的石頭之間升起,人群聚集觀看。","part":"A","sec":"Monuments, Architecture & Burial 古蹟、建築與墓葬","lab":"A146","t":"至"},{"w":"prehistoric","pos":"adj.","def":"from the time before writing was invented","cn":"史前的","s":"________ people painted animals on cave walls, and some of these paintings are more than thirty thousand years old.","zh":"史前人類在洞穴牆上畫了動物,其中一些畫已有三萬多年的歷史。","part":"A","sec":"Prehistoric Life & Early Humans 史前生活與早期人類","lab":"A147","t":"史前"},{"w":"Stone Age","pos":"n.phr.","def":"the early period when people used stone tools","cn":"石器時代","s":"People in the ________ ________ made tools from rocks, but they also used wood and bone for many jobs.","zh":"石器時代的人用石頭製作工具,但他們也用木頭和骨頭來做許多工作。","part":"A","sec":"Prehistoric Life & Early Humans 史前生活與早期人類","lab":"A148","t":"石器時代"},{"w":"Ice Age","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a long period when ice covered much of the Earth","cn":"冰河時期","s":"During the last ________ ________, sea levels were much lower, so people could walk from Asia to America.","zh":"在最後一次冰河時期,海平面低得多,所以人們能從亞洲走到美洲。","part":"A","sec":"Prehistoric Life & Early Humans 史前生活與早期人類","lab":"A149","t":"冰河時期"},{"w":"Neolithic","pos":"adj.","def":"from the later Stone Age when farming began","cn":"新石器時代的","s":"________ farmers built the first villages in Europe, and they kept sheep, goats and cattle.","zh":"新石器時代的農民在歐洲建立了第一批村莊,他們飼養綿羊、山羊和牛。","part":"A","sec":"Prehistoric Life & Early Humans 史前生活與早期人類","lab":"A150","t":"新石器時代的"},{"w":"hunter-gatherer","pos":"n.","def":"a person who lives by hunting animals and collecting plants","cn":"狩獵採集者","s":"A ________ had to move often to find food, so he could not carry many things with him.","zh":"狩獵採集者必須經常遷移來尋找食物,所以他無法隨身攜帶很多東西。","part":"A","sec":"Prehistoric Life & Early Humans 史前生活與早期人類","lab":"A151","t":"狩獵採集者"},{"w":"nomadic","pos":"adj.","def":"moving from place to place without a fixed home","cn":"遊牧的;流浪的","s":"The ________ people followed their animals across the grasslands, and they lived in tents that were easy to carry.","zh":"那些遊牧民族跟隨他們的牲畜穿越草原,住在容易攜帶的帳篷裡。","part":"A","sec":"Prehistoric Life & Early Humans 史前生活與早期人類","lab":"A152","t":"遊牧"},{"w":"tribe","pos":"n.","def":"a group of families with the same customs and leader","cn":"部落","s":"Each ________ had its own leader, but they sometimes met together to trade and celebrate.","zh":"每個部落都有自己的首領,但他們有時會聚在一起交易和慶祝。","part":"A","sec":"Prehistoric Life & Early Humans 史前生活與早期人類","lab":"A153","t":"部落"},{"w":"clan","pos":"n.","def":"a large group of related families","cn":"氏族;宗族","s":"Members of the same ________ shared the same family name, and they helped each other during hard winters.","zh":"同一氏族的成員擁有相同的姓氏,他們在艱困的冬天互相幫助。","part":"A","sec":"Prehistoric Life & Early Humans 史前生活與早期人類","lab":"A154","t":"氏族"},{"w":"kinship","pos":"n.","def":"a family relationship between people","cn":"親屬關係","s":"________ was very important in early societies, because your family decided where you lived and whom you married.","zh":"親屬關係在早期社會中非常重要,因為你的家族決定了你住在哪裡以及和誰結婚。","part":"A","sec":"Prehistoric Life & Early Humans 史前生活與早期人類","lab":"A155","t":"親屬關係"},{"w":"settler","pos":"n.","def":"a person who moves to a new place to live","cn":"移居者;殖民者","s":"The first ________ on the island built their homes near the beach, because the land inland was rocky.","zh":"島上的第一批移居者把家建在海灘附近,因為內陸的土地多岩石。","part":"A","sec":"Prehistoric Life & Early Humans 史前生活與早期人類","lab":"A156","t":"移居者"},{"w":"settlement","pos":"n.","def":"a place where people have come to live","cn":"聚落;定居點","s":"The remains of a small ________ were found by the lake, and it included ten round houses and a well.","zh":"在湖邊發現了一個小聚落的遺跡,包括十座圓形房屋和一口井。","part":"A","sec":"Prehistoric Life & Early Humans 史前生活與早期人類","lab":"A157","t":"聚落"},{"w":"hut","pos":"n.","def":"a small simple house","cn":"小屋;茅屋","s":"Each family lived in a small ________ made of wood and mud, and they cooked over a fire in the middle.","zh":"每個家庭住在用木頭和泥土搭成的小茅屋裡,他們在屋子中央生火煮飯。","part":"A","sec":"Prehistoric Life & Early Humans 史前生活與早期人類","lab":"A158","t":"茅屋"},{"w":"dwelling","pos":"n.","def":"a house or place where someone lives","cn":"住所;住處","s":"The cave was used as a ________ for thousands of years, and the floor was full of animal bones and ash.","zh":"這個洞穴被當作住所使用了數千年,地上滿是動物骨頭和灰燼。","part":"A","sec":"Prehistoric Life & Early Humans 史前生活與早期人類","lab":"A159","t":"住所"},{"w":"cave","pos":"n.","def":"a large hole in a hill or under the ground","cn":"洞穴","s":"Some children chased their dog into a ________, and they discovered amazing paintings on the walls.","zh":"幾個孩子追著他們的狗跑進一個洞穴,結果在牆上發現了驚人的壁畫。","part":"A","sec":"Prehistoric Life & Early Humans 史前生活與早期人類","lab":"A160","t":"洞穴"},{"w":"cave painting","pos":"n.phr.","def":"an ancient picture painted on the wall of a cave","cn":"洞穴壁畫","s":"The ________ ________ shows people hunting deer, so it gives us a clear idea of how they found food.","zh":"這幅洞穴壁畫描繪人們獵鹿的場景,所以它讓我們清楚了解他們如何取得食物。","part":"A","sec":"Prehistoric Life & Early Humans 史前生活與早期人類","lab":"A161","t":"洞穴壁畫"},{"w":"spear","pos":"n.","def":"a long stick with a sharp point used for hunting","cn":"矛;長矛","s":"The hunter threw his ________ at the deer, but it ran into the forest before he could catch it.","zh":"獵人把長矛擲向那隻鹿,但牠在他抓到之前就跑進了森林。","part":"A","sec":"Prehistoric Life & Early Humans 史前生活與早期人類","lab":"A162","t":"長矛"},{"w":"arrowhead","pos":"n.","def":"the sharp stone or metal point of an arrow","cn":"箭頭","s":"My uncle found a small stone ________ in his garden, and the museum said it was about five thousand years old.","zh":"我叔叔在他的花園裡發現了一個小石箭頭,博物館說它大約有五千年的歷史。","part":"A","sec":"Prehistoric Life & Early Humans 史前生活與早期人類","lab":"A163","t":"箭頭"},{"w":"axe","pos":"n.","def":"a tool with a heavy blade for cutting wood","cn":"斧頭","s":"Early farmers used a stone ________ to cut down trees, so they could clear the land for their crops.","zh":"早期農民用石斧砍伐樹木,這樣他們就能清出土地來種植作物。","part":"A","sec":"Prehistoric Life & Early Humans 史前生活與早期人類","lab":"A164","t":"斧"},{"w":"domesticate","pos":"v.","def":"to tame an animal or grow a plant for human use","cn":"馴化;馴養","s":"People began to ________ wild goats about ten thousand years ago, and this gave them a steady supply of milk.","zh":"人類大約在一萬年前開始馴化野山羊,這讓他們有穩定的乳汁來源。","part":"A","sec":"Prehistoric Life & Early Humans 史前生活與早期人類","lab":"A165","t":"馴化"},{"w":"agriculture","pos":"n.","def":"farming; growing crops and raising animals","cn":"農業","s":"The start of ________ changed human life completely, because people could stay in one place and build towns.","zh":"農業的開始徹底改變了人類生活,因為人們可以定居在一個地方並建立城鎮。","part":"A","sec":"Prehistoric Life & Early Humans 史前生活與早期人類","lab":"A166","t":"農業"},{"w":"sow / sowed / sown","pos":"v.","def":"to plant seeds in the ground","cn":"播種","s":"Early farmers ________ wheat in the autumn, and they harvested it in the summer when it turned golden.","zh":"早期農民在秋天播種小麥,並在夏天麥子轉為金黃時收割。","part":"A","sec":"Prehistoric Life & Early Humans 史前生活與早期人類","lab":"A167","t":"播種"},{"w":"grain","pos":"n.","def":"the seeds of crops like wheat and rice","cn":"穀物;穀粒","s":"The village stored its ________ in large clay jars, so families would have enough food during the winter.","zh":"村莊把穀物儲存在大陶罐裡,這樣家家戶戶在冬天就有足夠的食物。","part":"A","sec":"Prehistoric Life & Early Humans 史前生活與早期人類","lab":"A168","t":"穀物"},{"w":"plough","pos":"n.","def":"a farm tool used to turn over the soil","cn":"犁","s":"The invention of the ________ made farming much easier, because animals could now pull it through the fields.","zh":"犁的發明讓耕作容易得多,因為現在可以讓動物拉著它在田裡耕地。","part":"A","sec":"Prehistoric Life & Early Humans 史前生活與早期人類","lab":"A169","t":"犁"},{"w":"mammoth","pos":"n.","def":"a large hairy elephant that lived long ago","cn":"長毛象;猛獁象","s":"Hunters worked together to catch a ________, and one animal could feed a whole group for weeks.","zh":"獵人們合作捕捉一頭長毛象,一頭就能餵飽整個群體好幾個星期。","part":"A","sec":"Prehistoric Life & Early Humans 史前生活與早期人類","lab":"A170","t":"長毛象"},{"w":"hearth","pos":"n.","def":"the area around a fire in a home","cn":"爐床;火爐邊","s":"The family sat around the ________ every evening, and the older people told stories to the children.","zh":"一家人每天晚上圍坐在火爐邊,年長的人講故事給孩子們聽。","part":"A","sec":"Prehistoric Life & Early Humans 史前生活與早期人類","lab":"A171","t":"火爐邊"},{"w":"ancestor","pos":"n.","def":"a family member who lived long before you","cn":"祖先","s":"Many families visit the graves of their ________ every year, because they want to show respect to them.","zh":"許多家庭每年都會去掃祖先的墓,因為他們想表達對祖先的敬意。","part":"A","sec":"Prehistoric Life & Early Humans 史前生活與早期人類","lab":"A172","t":"祖先"},{"w":"skull","pos":"n.","def":"the bones of the head","cn":"頭骨;顱骨","s":"The ________ found in the cave belonged to a young woman, and scientists used it to rebuild her face.","zh":"在洞穴中發現的頭骨屬於一名年輕女子,科學家用它來重建她的臉孔。","part":"A","sec":"Prehistoric Life & Early Humans 史前生活與早期人類","lab":"A173","t":"頭骨"},{"w":"primitive","pos":"adj.","def":"simple and from an early stage of development","cn":"原始的;簡陋的","s":"The tools looked ________, but they were actually very well designed for cutting meat and cleaning animal skins.","zh":"這些工具看起來很原始,但它們其實設計得非常適合切肉和清理獸皮。","part":"A","sec":"Prehistoric Life & Early Humans 史前生活與早期人類","lab":"A174","t":"原始"},{"w":"merchant","pos":"n.","def":"a person who buys and sells goods, often abroad","cn":"商人","s":"The ________ travelled for months to sell his cloth, and he came home with spices, gold and stories.","zh":"那位商人旅行了好幾個月去賣他的布料,回家時帶著香料、黃金和許多故事。","part":"A","sec":"Trade, Seafaring & Conflict 貿易、航海與衝突","lab":"A175","t":"商人"},{"w":"barter","pos":"v.","def":"to exchange goods without using money","cn":"以物易物","s":"Before coins existed, people would ________ grain for tools, so a farmer could get an axe for a bag of wheat.","zh":"在錢幣出現之前,人們會用穀物交換工具,所以農夫可以用一袋小麥換一把斧頭。","part":"A","sec":"Trade, Seafaring & Conflict 貿易、航海與衝突","lab":"A176","t":"交換"},{"w":"coin","pos":"n.","def":"a small round piece of metal used as money","cn":"硬幣;錢幣","s":"The ________ shows the face of an emperor, so experts know exactly when it was made.","zh":"這枚錢幣上有一位皇帝的頭像,所以專家確切知道它是何時鑄造的。","part":"A","sec":"Trade, Seafaring & Conflict 貿易、航海與衝突","lab":"A177","t":"錢幣"},{"w":"caravan","pos":"n.","def":"a group of traders travelling together, often with camels","cn":"商隊;駝隊","s":"A long ________ of camels crossed the desert, and it carried silk, spices and glass to distant markets.","zh":"一支長長的駱駝商隊穿越沙漠,運送絲綢、香料和玻璃到遙遠的市場。","part":"A","sec":"Trade, Seafaring & Conflict 貿易、航海與衝突","lab":"A178","t":"商隊"},{"w":"Silk Road","pos":"n.phr.","def":"ancient trade routes linking China and Europe","cn":"絲路","s":"The ________ ________ connected China with Europe, so ideas and inventions spread along with goods.","zh":"絲路連接了中國和歐洲,所以思想和發明隨著商品一起傳播。","part":"A","sec":"Trade, Seafaring & Conflict 貿易、航海與衝突","lab":"A179","t":"絲路"},{"w":"spice","pos":"n.","def":"a dried plant part used to add flavour to food","cn":"香料","s":"Pepper was once a very expensive ________, and sailors risked their lives to bring it from Asia.","zh":"胡椒曾經是一種非常昂貴的香料,水手們冒著生命危險從亞洲把它運回來。","part":"A","sec":"Trade, Seafaring & Conflict 貿易、航海與衝突","lab":"A180","t":"香料"},{"w":"amber","pos":"n.","def":"hard yellow stone made from old tree resin","cn":"琥珀","s":"Beads made of ________ were traded across Europe, and some pieces even contain tiny insects from millions of years ago.","zh":"琥珀製的珠子在歐洲各地交易,有些甚至含有數百萬年前的小昆蟲。","part":"A","sec":"Trade, Seafaring & Conflict 貿易、航海與衝突","lab":"A181","t":"琥珀"},{"w":"pirate","pos":"n.","def":"a person who attacks and robs ships at sea","cn":"海盜","s":"Mediterranean ________ often attacked trading ships near the islands, so merchants usually travelled in groups for safety.","zh":"地中海海盜常在島嶼附近攻擊貿易船隻,所以商人們通常結伴航行以策安全。","part":"A","sec":"Trade, Seafaring & Conflict 貿易、航海與衝突","lab":"A182","t":"海盜"},{"w":"galley","pos":"n.","def":"an ancient ship moved by oars and sails","cn":"划槳帆船;槳帆船","s":"The ________ had more than a hundred rowers, and it could move fast even when there was no wind.","zh":"這艘槳帆船有一百多名划槳手,即使沒有風也能快速前進。","part":"A","sec":"Trade, Seafaring & Conflict 貿易、航海與衝突","lab":"A183","t":"槳帆船"},{"w":"oar","pos":"n.","def":"a long pole with a flat end used to row a boat","cn":"槳","s":"Each rower held a heavy ________, and they moved together to the beat of a drum.","zh":"每位划槳手握著一支沉重的槳,他們隨著鼓聲一起划動。","part":"A","sec":"Trade, Seafaring & Conflict 貿易、航海與衝突","lab":"A184","t":"槳"},{"w":"sail","pos":"n.","def":"a large cloth that catches the wind to move a ship","cn":"帆","s":"The ship raised its ________ when the wind became strong, so the tired rowers could finally rest.","zh":"風變強時船升起了帆,所以疲憊的划槳手終於可以休息了。","part":"A","sec":"Trade, Seafaring & Conflict 貿易、航海與衝突","lab":"A185","t":"帆"},{"w":"seafaring","pos":"adj.","def":"travelling regularly by sea","cn":"航海的","s":"The Phoenicians were a ________ people, and they set up trading ports all around the Mediterranean Sea.","zh":"腓尼基人是一個航海民族,他們在地中海沿岸各地建立了貿易港口。","part":"A","sec":"Trade, Seafaring & Conflict 貿易、航海與衝突","lab":"A186","t":"航海"},{"w":"shipbuilding","pos":"n.","def":"the work of building ships","cn":"造船(業)","s":"The town was famous for ________, so wood was brought from distant forests to make strong boats.","zh":"這個城鎮以造船業聞名,所以人們從遙遠的森林運來木材製造堅固的船隻。","part":"A","sec":"Trade, Seafaring & Conflict 貿易、航海與衝突","lab":"A187","t":"造船業"},{"w":"colonise","pos":"v.","def":"to take control of a place and send people to live there","cn":"殖民;移居","s":"The Greeks began to ________ islands across the sea, because there was not enough farmland at home.","zh":"希臘人開始在海上各島殖民,因為本土沒有足夠的農地。","part":"A","sec":"Trade, Seafaring & Conflict 貿易、航海與衝突","lab":"A188","t":"殖民"},{"w":"invade","pos":"v.","def":"to enter a country with an army to take control","cn":"入侵;侵略","s":"The enemy decided to ________ in winter, because they knew the river would be frozen and easy to cross.","zh":"敵人決定在冬天入侵,因為他們知道河流會結冰而容易渡過。","part":"A","sec":"Trade, Seafaring & Conflict 貿易、航海與衝突","lab":"A189","t":"入侵"},{"w":"conquer","pos":"v.","def":"to take control of a place by force","cn":"征服","s":"Alexander the Great managed to ________ a huge area, but his empire broke apart soon after he died.","zh":"亞歷山大大帝成功征服了廣大的地區,但他死後不久帝國就分裂了。","part":"A","sec":"Trade, Seafaring & Conflict 貿易、航海與衝突","lab":"A190","t":"征服"},{"w":"siege","pos":"n.","def":"surrounding a city to force it to give up","cn":"圍城;圍攻","s":"The ________ lasted for ten months, and the people inside the walls had to eat rats to survive.","zh":"這場圍城持續了十個月,城牆內的人們必須吃老鼠才能活下去。","part":"A","sec":"Trade, Seafaring & Conflict 貿易、航海與衝突","lab":"A191","t":"圍城"},{"w":"fortress","pos":"n.","def":"a strong building used for military defence","cn":"堡壘;要塞","s":"The ________ was built on a cliff above the sea, so attackers could not reach it easily.","zh":"這座堡壘建在海上的懸崖上,所以攻擊者無法輕易接近它。","part":"A","sec":"Trade, Seafaring & Conflict 貿易、航海與衝突","lab":"A192","t":"堡壘"},{"w":"armour","pos":"n.","def":"metal clothing worn to protect the body in battle","cn":"盔甲","s":"The knight's ________ was so heavy that he needed help to climb onto his horse.","zh":"那位騎士的盔甲非常沉重,所以他需要別人幫忙才能爬上馬。","part":"A","sec":"Trade, Seafaring & Conflict 貿易、航海與衝突","lab":"A193","t":"盔甲"},{"w":"sword","pos":"n.","def":"a weapon with a long metal blade","cn":"劍","s":"The ________ was found in a river, and experts believe it was thrown there as a gift to the gods.","zh":"這把劍是在河裡發現的,專家相信它是被當作獻給神明的禮物丟進去的。","part":"A","sec":"Trade, Seafaring & Conflict 貿易、航海與衝突","lab":"A194","t":"劍"},{"w":"warrior","pos":"n.","def":"a brave fighter, especially in ancient times","cn":"戰士;勇士","s":"The ________ was buried with his sword and shield, so archaeologists knew he was an important fighter.","zh":"這名戰士與他的劍和盾牌一起下葬,所以考古學家知道他是一位重要的戰士。","part":"A","sec":"Trade, Seafaring & Conflict 貿易、航海與衝突","lab":"A195","t":"戰士"},{"w":"battlefield","pos":"n.","def":"the place where a battle is fought","cn":"戰場","s":"Metal arrowheads were found all over the ________, and they helped historians understand how the battle took place.","zh":"在整個戰場上都發現了金屬箭頭,它們幫助歷史學家了解這場戰役是如何進行的。","part":"A","sec":"Trade, Seafaring & Conflict 貿易、航海與衝突","lab":"A196","t":"戰場"},{"w":"plunder","pos":"v.","def":"to steal goods by force, especially in war","cn":"掠奪;搶劫","s":"The invaders tried to ________ the temple's gold, but the priests had hidden it in a secret room.","zh":"入侵者試圖掠奪神廟的黃金,但祭司們已經把它藏在一間密室裡。","part":"A","sec":"Trade, Seafaring & Conflict 貿易、航海與衝突","lab":"A197","t":"掠奪"},{"w":"revolt","pos":"n.","def":"an attempt by people to fight against their rulers","cn":"叛亂;起義","s":"The peasants started a ________ because taxes were too high, but the army stopped it within a month.","zh":"農民們因為稅太重而發動起義,但軍隊在一個月內就鎮壓了。","part":"A","sec":"Trade, Seafaring & Conflict 貿易、航海與衝突","lab":"A198","t":"起義"},{"w":"alliance","pos":"n.","def":"an agreement between groups to support each other","cn":"聯盟;同盟","s":"The two cities formed an ________ against their common enemy, and together they won the war.","zh":"這兩座城市結成聯盟對抗共同的敵人,並一起贏得了戰爭。","part":"A","sec":"Trade, Seafaring & Conflict 貿易、航海與衝突","lab":"A199","t":"聯盟"},{"w":"downfall","pos":"n.","def":"the loss of power or success","cn":"垮台;衰敗","s":"Bad harvests and endless wars led to the ________ of the empire, so its great cities slowly became empty.","zh":"歉收和無休止的戰爭導致帝國的衰敗,所以它的偉大城市漸漸變得空蕩。","part":"A","sec":"Trade, Seafaring & Conflict 貿易、航海與衝突","lab":"A200","t":"衰敗"},{"w":"accrue","pos":"v.","def":"to increase or build up gradually over time","cn":"累積;逐漸增加","s":"Layers of mud began to ________ over the old city, so after many centuries it was completely hidden underground.","zh":"一層層的泥土開始在古城上累積,所以經過許多世紀後它完全被埋在地下。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B1","t":"累積"},{"w":"adorn","pos":"v.","def":"to decorate something to make it beautiful","cn":"裝飾;點綴","s":"Ancient Egyptians liked to ________ their tombs with bright paintings, and many of the colours are still clear today.","zh":"古埃及人喜歡用鮮豔的圖畫裝飾他們的墳墓,其中許多顏色至今仍然清晰。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B2","t":"裝飾"},{"w":"ascend","pos":"v.","def":"to go up or climb","cn":"登上;上升","s":"Visitors must ________ more than two hundred steps to reach the top of the temple, but the view is worth the effort.","zh":"遊客必須登上兩百多級台階才能到達神廟頂端,但那景色值得這番努力。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B3","t":"登上"},{"w":"bequeath","pos":"v.","def":"to leave something to someone after you die","cn":"遺贈;遺留給","s":"The rich collector decided to ________ his ancient coins to the museum, so everyone could enjoy them.","zh":"這位富有的收藏家決定把他的古錢幣遺贈給博物館,讓每個人都能欣賞。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B4","t":"遺贈"},{"w":"chronicle","pos":"v.","def":"to record events in the order they happened","cn":"記錄;編年記載","s":"Monks used to ________ every important event in the kingdom, and their books are now valuable to historians.","zh":"修道士過去會記錄王國中每一件重要的事,他們的書現在對歷史學家非常珍貴。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B5","t":"記錄"},{"w":"commemorate","pos":"v.","def":"to do something special to remember a person or event","cn":"紀念","s":"The city built a statue to ________ the famous queen, and people place flowers there every year.","zh":"市政府建造了一座雕像來紀念那位著名的女王,人們每年都會在那裡獻花。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B6","t":"紀念"},{"w":"contest","pos":"v.","def":"to argue that something is wrong or not true","cn":"質疑;爭辯","s":"Some historians ________ the idea that the city was destroyed by war, because they found no weapons there.","zh":"一些歷史學家質疑這座城市是被戰爭摧毀的說法,因為他們在那裡沒有找到武器。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B7","t":"質疑"},{"w":"deface","pos":"v.","def":"to damage the surface of something, especially by writing on it","cn":"塗污;損毀(外觀)","s":"Some tourists ________ the ancient walls with their names, so the government now fines anyone who does this.","zh":"一些遊客在古老的牆上寫名字而毀損了它們,所以政府現在對任何這樣做的人處以罰款。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B8","t":"毀損"},{"w":"descend","pos":"v.","def":"to go down","cn":"下降;走下","s":"We had to ________ a narrow staircase into the tomb, and the air became cooler with every step.","zh":"我們必須走下一道狹窄的樓梯進入墳墓,每走一步空氣就變得更涼。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B9","t":"走下"},{"w":"dwell","pos":"v.","def":"to live in a place","cn":"居住","s":"People used to ________ in these caves during the winter, but they moved to the river valley in summer.","zh":"人們過去冬天居住在這些洞穴裡,但夏天會搬到河谷。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B10","t":"居住"},{"w":"eclipse","pos":"v.","def":"to become more important or successful than something else","cn":"使黯然失色;超越","s":"The new port began to ________ the old trading town, so many merchants packed up and moved away.","zh":"新港口開始使舊的貿易城鎮黯然失色,所以許多商人收拾行李搬走了。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B11","t":"使 黯然失色"},{"w":"ensue","pos":"v.","def":"to happen after or as a result of something","cn":"接著發生;隨之而來","s":"When the king died without a son, a long fight for power began to ________, and the kingdom was divided.","zh":"當國王死時沒有兒子,一場漫長的權力爭奪隨之而來,王國也因此分裂。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B12","t":"隨之而來"},{"w":"erect","pos":"v.","def":"to build or put up something tall","cn":"豎立;建造","s":"Ancient people managed to ________ huge stones in a circle, although they had no machines or metal tools.","zh":"古人成功地把巨石豎立成一圈,雖然他們沒有機器或金屬工具。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B13","t":"豎立"},{"w":"extinguish","pos":"v.","def":"to put out a fire or end something","cn":"熄滅;撲滅","s":"The villagers tried to ________ the fire with river water, but the wooden temple burned to the ground.","zh":"村民們試著用河水撲滅火勢,但那座木造神廟還是被燒成平地。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B14","t":"撲滅"},{"w":"glorify","pos":"v.","def":"to praise someone and make them seem better than they are","cn":"美化;頌揚","s":"Old paintings often ________ the king as a great hero, although historians know he lost many battles.","zh":"古老的畫作常常把國王美化成偉大的英雄,雖然歷史學家知道他輸了許多戰役。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B15","t":"美化"},{"w":"immortalise","pos":"v.","def":"to make someone famous for a very long time","cn":"使不朽;使流芳百世","s":"The poet wanted to ________ the brave soldiers in his poem, and people still read it two thousand years later.","zh":"詩人想在他的詩中使那些勇敢的士兵永垂不朽,兩千年後人們仍然在讀這首詩。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B16","t":"使 永垂不朽"},{"w":"inherit","pos":"v.","def":"to receive money or property from someone who has died","cn":"繼承","s":"The young prince would ________ the throne when his father died, so he was trained to rule from childhood.","zh":"年輕的王子將在父親去世後繼承王位,所以他從小就接受統治的訓練。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B17","t":"繼承"},{"w":"lament","pos":"v.","def":"to feel or say that you are very sad about something","cn":"哀悼;悲嘆","s":"Many local people ________ the loss of the old market, because it was replaced by a modern shopping centre.","zh":"許多當地人哀嘆老市集的消失,因為它被一座現代購物中心取代了。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B18","t":"哀嘆"},{"w":"linger","pos":"v.","def":"to stay for a long time","cn":"徘徊;逗留;久久不散","s":"Visitors often ________ in front of the golden mask, because it is the most beautiful object in the museum.","zh":"參觀者常常在黃金面具前逗留,因為它是博物館裡最美的物品。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B19","t":"逗留"},{"w":"mar","pos":"v.","def":"to spoil or damage something","cn":"損壞;破壞","s":"Ugly modern buildings ________ the view of the ancient castle, so many tourists feel disappointed when they arrive.","zh":"醜陋的現代建築破壞了古堡的景觀,所以許多遊客抵達時都感到失望。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B20","t":"破壞"},{"w":"narrate","pos":"v.","def":"to tell a story or describe events","cn":"敘述;講述","s":"An actor will ________ the history of the city during the light show, and the story will be shown on the old walls.","zh":"一位演員將在燈光秀期間講述這座城市的歷史,故事會投影在古老的城牆上。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B21","t":"講述"},{"w":"obliterate","pos":"v.","def":"to destroy something completely","cn":"徹底摧毀;抹去","s":"The volcano managed to ________ the town in a single day, but the ash also preserved many buildings perfectly.","zh":"火山在一天之內就徹底摧毀了這座城鎮,但火山灰也完整地保存了許多建築。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B22","t":"徹底摧毀"},{"w":"overrun / overran / overrun","pos":"v.","def":"to spread over a place in large numbers","cn":"侵佔;蔓延","s":"After the people left, wild plants ________ the city, and the temples were hidden by trees for centuries.","zh":"人們離開後,野生植物蔓延整座城市,神廟被樹木遮蓋了好幾個世紀。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B23","t":"蔓延"},{"w":"perish","pos":"v.","def":"to die, especially in a terrible way","cn":"死亡;喪生","s":"Thousands of people ________ when the volcano erupted, because they did not have enough time to escape.","zh":"火山爆發時數千人喪生,因為他們沒有足夠的時間逃離。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B24","t":"喪生"},{"w":"proclaim","pos":"v.","def":"to announce something officially and publicly","cn":"宣布;宣告","s":"After the battle, the general decided to ________ himself emperor, but many soldiers refused to follow him.","zh":"戰役結束後,那位將軍決定宣布自己為皇帝,但許多士兵拒絕追隨他。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B25","t":"宣布"},{"w":"ransack","pos":"v.","def":"to search a place roughly and steal things","cn":"洗劫;搜劫","s":"Robbers ________ the tomb long ago, so archaeologists found only broken pots and a few small beads.","zh":"盜墓者很久以前就洗劫了這座墳墓,所以考古學家只找到破碎的陶罐和幾顆小珠子。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B26","t":"洗劫"},{"w":"raze","pos":"v.","def":"to completely destroy a building or town","cn":"夷為平地","s":"The invaders tried to ________ the city to the ground, but some of its strong stone walls survived.","zh":"入侵者試圖把這座城市夷為平地,但它一些堅固的石牆倖存了下來。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B27","t":"夷為平地"},{"w":"recount","pos":"v.","def":"to tell someone about something that happened","cn":"敘述;講述","s":"The old sailor liked to ________ stories about his voyages, and the children listened with wide eyes.","zh":"老水手喜歡講述他航行的故事,孩子們睜大眼睛聽著。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B28","t":"講述"},{"w":"rediscover","pos":"v.","def":"to find something again after it was lost or forgotten","cn":"重新發現","s":"Explorers managed to ________ the lost city in 1911, although local farmers had known about it for years.","zh":"探險家在1911年重新發現了這座失落之城,雖然當地農民多年來早已知道它的存在。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B29","t":"重新發現"},{"w":"repurpose","pos":"v.","def":"to use something for a new purpose","cn":"改作他用;重新利用","s":"The town decided to ________ the old prison as a history museum, so visitors can now explore its dark cells.","zh":"小鎮決定把舊監獄改作歷史博物館,所以遊客現在可以探索它陰暗的牢房。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B30","t":"改作"},{"w":"resurrect","pos":"v.","def":"to bring something back into use or existence","cn":"復興;使復活","s":"Historians tried to ________ ancient recipes, and they cooked bread exactly as the Romans did.","zh":"歷史學家試圖復原古代食譜,他們完全按照羅馬人的方式烤麵包。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B31","t":"復原"},{"w":"revere","pos":"v.","def":"to respect and admire someone or something deeply","cn":"崇敬;尊崇","s":"The local people ________ the old tree as a sacred symbol, so nobody is allowed to cut its branches.","zh":"當地人把那棵老樹尊崇為神聖的象徵,所以沒有人被允許砍它的樹枝。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B32","t":"尊崇"},{"w":"situate","pos":"v.","def":"to build or place something in a particular position","cn":"使位於;坐落於","s":"The ancient people chose to ________ their village on a hill, because it was safer from floods and enemies.","zh":"古人選擇把他們的村莊建在山丘上,因為那裡比較不會受洪水和敵人侵擾。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B33","t":"建在"},{"w":"supplant","pos":"v.","def":"to take the place of something older","cn":"取代","s":"Iron tools began to ________ bronze ones, because iron was easier to find and much stronger.","zh":"鐵器開始取代青銅器,因為鐵比較容易取得而且堅固得多。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B34","t":"取代"},{"w":"surmise","pos":"v.","def":"to guess something without much evidence","cn":"推測;猜測","s":"From the size of the house, we can ________ that a rich family lived there, but we do not know their names.","zh":"從房子的大小,我們可以推測那裡住過一個富有的家庭,但我們不知道他們的名字。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B35","t":"推測"},{"w":"testify","pos":"v.","def":"to show that something is true","cn":"證明;作證","s":"The beautiful gold jewellery seems to ________ to the wealth of the city, so it must have been a busy trading centre.","zh":"這些美麗的金飾似乎證明了這座城市的富裕,所以它一定曾是繁忙的貿易中心。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B36","t":"證明"},{"w":"topple","pos":"v.","def":"to make something or someone fall","cn":"推翻;推倒","s":"Angry citizens tried to ________ the cruel ruler, and they pulled down his statue in the main square.","zh":"憤怒的市民試圖推翻殘暴的統治者,他們在主廣場上拉倒了他的雕像。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B37","t":"推翻"},{"w":"uproot","pos":"v.","def":"to make people leave their home and move far away","cn":"使離開家園;連根拔起","s":"The war managed to ________ thousands of families, so whole villages were empty for many years.","zh":"戰爭讓數千個家庭被迫離開家園,所以整個村莊空了好多年。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B38","t":"被迫離開家園"},{"w":"wield","pos":"v.","def":"to have and use power or a weapon","cn":"行使(權力);揮舞","s":"Priests used to ________ great power in ancient Egypt, and even kings asked them for advice.","zh":"在古埃及,祭司過去握有很大的權力,連國王都會向他們請教。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B39","t":"握有"},{"w":"abound","pos":"v.","def":"to exist in large numbers","cn":"大量存在;充滿","s":"Stories about hidden treasure ________ in this region, so treasure hunters often visit with metal tools.","zh":"這個地區充滿有關隱藏寶藏的故事,所以尋寶者常帶著金屬工具來訪。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B40","t":"充滿"},{"w":"amalgamate","pos":"v.","def":"to join two or more things together into one","cn":"合併;融合","s":"The two kingdoms decided to ________ through marriage, and the new country became the strongest in the region.","zh":"這兩個王國決定透過聯姻合併,而新的國家成為該地區最強大的國家。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B41","t":"合併"},{"w":"annex","pos":"v.","def":"to take control of a country or area and add it to your own","cn":"併吞;吞併","s":"The emperor tried to ________ the small island, because it was an important stop for trading ships.","zh":"皇帝試圖併吞那座小島,因為它是貿易船隻的重要中繼站。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B42","t":"併吞"},{"w":"archive","pos":"v.","def":"to store documents or records in an organised way","cn":"將…歸檔保存","s":"The library will ________ the old letters in a safe room, and students can read digital copies online.","zh":"圖書館會把這些舊信件歸檔保存在安全的房間裡,學生可以在網路上閱讀數位副本。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B43","t":"歸檔保存"},{"w":"betray","pos":"v.","def":"to be disloyal to someone who trusts you","cn":"背叛;出賣","s":"The general decided to ________ his king, and he opened the city gates to the enemy at night.","zh":"那位將軍決定背叛他的國王,他在夜裡為敵人打開了城門。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B44","t":"背叛"},{"w":"crumble","pos":"v.","def":"to break into small pieces slowly","cn":"崩塌;碎裂","s":"The old walls began to ________ after centuries of rain, so workers are now repairing them stone by stone.","zh":"經過幾個世紀的雨水沖刷,古老的城牆開始崩塌,所以工人們正在一塊一塊地修補。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B45","t":"崩塌"},{"w":"decree","pos":"v.","def":"to give an official order","cn":"頒布;下令","s":"The emperor ________ that everyone must use the same weights and measures, so trade became easier across the land.","zh":"皇帝下令每個人都必須使用相同的度量衡,所以全國的貿易變得更加容易。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B46","t":"下令"},{"w":"disintegrate","pos":"v.","def":"to break into many small parts","cn":"瓦解;碎裂","s":"The old paper can ________ if you touch it, so the experts wear gloves and use special tools.","zh":"那些古老的紙張一碰就可能碎裂,所以專家們戴著手套並使用特殊工具。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B47","t":"碎裂"},{"w":"embellish","pos":"v.","def":"to add details to a story to make it more interesting","cn":"潤飾;添油加醋","s":"Storytellers often ________ old legends with magic and monsters, so it is hard to know what really happened.","zh":"說書人常常在古老的傳說中添加魔法和怪物,所以很難知道真正發生了什麼事。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B48","t":"添加"},{"w":"enshrine","pos":"v.","def":"to protect an idea or right, often in law","cn":"載入(法律);奉為神聖","s":"The new law will ________ the protection of ancient sites, so nobody can build on them without permission.","zh":"新法律將把古蹟保護明文載入,所以未經許可任何人都不能在上面建造。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B49","t":"明文載入"},{"w":"exile","pos":"v.","def":"to force someone to leave their country","cn":"流放;放逐","s":"The new king decided to ________ his brother to a distant island, because he was afraid of losing his throne.","zh":"新國王決定把他的弟弟流放到遙遠的島上,因為他害怕失去王位。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B50","t":"流放"},{"w":"falsify","pos":"v.","def":"to change records to trick people","cn":"竄改;偽造","s":"Some officials used to ________ the tax records, so the emperor received much less gold than he expected.","zh":"一些官員過去會竄改稅收紀錄,所以皇帝收到的黃金比他預期的少得多。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B51","t":"竄改"},{"w":"govern","pos":"v.","def":"to officially control a country or area","cn":"統治;治理","s":"The emperor sent his sons to ________ the far provinces, but they often fought with each other.","zh":"皇帝派他的兒子們去治理遙遠的省份,但他們常常互相爭鬥。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B52","t":"治理"},{"w":"herald","pos":"v.","def":"to be a sign that something is going to happen","cn":"預示;宣告…的到來","s":"The invention of writing seemed to ________ a new age, because laws and stories could now be kept forever.","zh":"文字的發明似乎預示了一個新時代,因為法律和故事現在可以永久保存。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B53","t":"預示"},{"w":"idealise","pos":"v.","def":"to think that something is better than it really is","cn":"理想化","s":"People often ________ life in ancient times, but most people worked very hard and died young.","zh":"人們常常把古代生活理想化,但大多數人工作非常辛苦而且很年輕就去世。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B54","t":"理想化"},{"w":"inaugurate","pos":"v.","def":"to open a new building or start something officially","cn":"為…舉行落成典禮;開創","s":"The mayor will ________ the new museum next month, and entry will be free for the first week.","zh":"市長將在下個月為新博物館舉行開幕典禮,第一週入場免費。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B55","t":"舉行開幕典禮"},{"w":"incite","pos":"v.","def":"to encourage people to be violent or angry","cn":"煽動;激起","s":"The rebel leader tried to ________ the peasants against the king, so soldiers were sent to arrest him.","zh":"叛軍首領試圖煽動農民反抗國王,所以士兵被派去逮捕他。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B56","t":"煽動"},{"w":"mingle","pos":"v.","def":"to mix together","cn":"混合;交融","s":"In busy ports, many cultures began to ________, so the food, music and languages became very rich.","zh":"在繁忙的港口,許多文化開始交融,所以食物、音樂和語言都變得非常豐富。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B57","t":"交融"},{"w":"oppress","pos":"v.","def":"to treat a group of people cruelly and unfairly","cn":"壓迫","s":"The cruel ruler continued to ________ the farmers with high taxes, so many of them ran away to the mountains.","zh":"那位殘暴的統治者持續用重稅壓迫農民,所以許多人逃到了山裡。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B58","t":"壓迫"},{"w":"outlive","pos":"v.","def":"to live longer than someone or something","cn":"比…活得長;比…存在更久","s":"Good stone buildings can ________ the people who built them by thousands of years, and the pyramids are a great example.","zh":"好的石造建築能比建造它們的人存在更久好幾千年,而金字塔就是一個絕佳的例子。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B59","t":"比 存在更久"},{"w":"overthrow / overthrew / overthrown","pos":"v.","def":"to remove a ruler from power by force","cn":"推翻","s":"The soldiers ________ the emperor in a single night, and they chose a new leader from their own army.","zh":"士兵們在一夜之間推翻了皇帝,並從自己的軍隊中選出了新的領袖。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B60","t":"推翻"},{"w":"predate","pos":"v.","def":"to exist earlier than something else","cn":"早於;先於","s":"The stone circle seems to ________ the pyramids by several hundred years, so it is even older than people thought.","zh":"這個石圈似乎早於金字塔好幾百年,所以它比人們以為的還要古老。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B61","t":"早於"},{"w":"reclaim","pos":"v.","def":"to get back something that was taken from you","cn":"收回;討回","s":"Several countries want to ________ ancient objects from foreign museums, because they believe these treasures belong at home.","zh":"好幾個國家想從外國博物館收回古代文物,因為他們認為這些寶物屬於自己的國家。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B62","t":"收回"},{"w":"reinstate","pos":"v.","def":"to put someone or something back in its old position","cn":"恢復(原職或原狀)","s":"After the war, the people chose to ________ the old king, because the new ruler had been cruel.","zh":"戰後,人民選擇恢復舊國王的王位,因為新統治者很殘暴。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B63","t":"恢復"},{"w":"renounce","pos":"v.","def":"to officially give up a right or position","cn":"宣布放棄","s":"The prince chose to ________ his right to the throne, so he could marry the woman he loved.","zh":"王子選擇放棄他的王位繼承權,這樣他就能和他心愛的女子結婚。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B64","t":"放棄"},{"w":"resemble","pos":"v.","def":"to look like or be similar to something","cn":"類似;像","s":"The ancient tools ________ modern kitchen knives, so it is easy to guess what they were used for.","zh":"這些古代工具很像現代的菜刀,所以很容易猜到它們的用途。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B65","t":"像"},{"w":"resist","pos":"v.","def":"to fight against something or refuse to accept it","cn":"抵抗;反抗","s":"The small town managed to ________ the invaders for months, but finally it ran out of food and water.","zh":"這個小鎮成功抵抗入侵者好幾個月,但最終耗盡了食物和水。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B66","t":"抵抗"},{"w":"retreat","pos":"v.","def":"to move back, especially in a battle","cn":"撤退","s":"The army had to ________ when winter came, because the soldiers did not have warm clothes or enough food.","zh":"冬天來臨時軍隊必須撤退,因為士兵們沒有保暖的衣服或足夠的食物。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B67","t":"撤退"},{"w":"revolve","pos":"v.","def":"to have something as the main subject or centre","cn":"圍繞;以…為中心","s":"Life in the village used to ________ around the harvest, so everyone helped in the fields during autumn.","zh":"過去村莊的生活圍繞著收成,所以秋天每個人都會到田裡幫忙。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B68","t":"圍繞"},{"w":"scatter","pos":"v.","def":"to spread things over a wide area","cn":"散落;分散","s":"The storm seemed to ________ the ship's cargo across the seabed, so divers found jars over a large area.","zh":"暴風雨似乎把船上的貨物散落在整片海床上,所以潛水員在大範圍內發現了陶罐。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B69","t":"散落"},{"w":"subside","pos":"v.","def":"to become less strong or return to normal","cn":"平息;消退","s":"When the floods began to ________, the villagers returned and found that their houses were covered in mud.","zh":"洪水開始消退時,村民們回到家,發現房子都被泥巴覆蓋了。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B70","t":"消退"},{"w":"surrender","pos":"v.","def":"to stop fighting and accept defeat","cn":"投降","s":"The city decided to ________ after a long siege, because the people inside were starving.","zh":"經過長時間的圍城,這座城市決定投降,因為城內的人們正在挨餓。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B71","t":"投降"},{"w":"tarnish","pos":"v.","def":"to make something less bright or damage a reputation","cn":"使失去光澤;玷污","s":"Silver coins ________ quickly in damp air, so the museum keeps them in special dry cases.","zh":"銀幣在潮濕的空氣中很快就會失去光澤,所以博物館把它們存放在特殊的乾燥櫃中。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B72","t":"失去光澤"},{"w":"thwart","pos":"v.","def":"to stop someone from doing what they planned","cn":"阻撓;挫敗","s":"Guards managed to ________ the robbers' plan, so the golden statues stayed safely inside the temple.","zh":"警衛成功挫敗了盜賊的計畫,所以黃金雕像安全地留在神廟裡。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B73","t":"挫敗"},{"w":"affinity","pos":"n.","def":"a natural liking for or connection with something","cn":"親近感;相似性","s":"The two ancient languages show a strong ________ with each other, so experts believe they came from the same source.","zh":"這兩種古代語言彼此顯示出很強的相似性,所以專家相信它們來自同一個源頭。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B74","t":"相似性"},{"w":"allegiance","pos":"n.","def":"loyalty to a leader, country or group","cn":"忠誠;效忠","s":"The soldiers swore ________ to the new king, but some of them secretly supported his brother.","zh":"士兵們宣誓效忠新國王,但其中一些人暗中支持他的弟弟。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B75","t":"效忠"},{"w":"anarchy","pos":"n.","def":"a situation with no government or order","cn":"無政府狀態;混亂","s":"After the emperor was killed, the country fell into ________, and robbers controlled many of the roads.","zh":"皇帝被殺後,國家陷入了無政府狀態,盜匪控制了許多道路。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B76","t":"無政府狀態"},{"w":"antecedent","pos":"n.","def":"something that existed before and influenced something later","cn":"前身;先例","s":"The ancient Greek theatre is an ________ of modern drama, so many plays today still follow its rules.","zh":"古希臘劇場是現代戲劇的前身,所以今天許多戲劇仍然遵循它的規則。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B77","t":"前身"},{"w":"apex","pos":"n.","def":"the highest point of something","cn":"頂點;巔峰","s":"The empire reached its ________ around the year 100, but it slowly grew weaker after that.","zh":"這個帝國大約在西元100年達到巔峰,但之後逐漸衰弱。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B78","t":"巔峰"},{"w":"artistry","pos":"n.","def":"great skill in creating something beautiful","cn":"藝術技巧;藝術才能","s":"The ________ of the golden mask amazed the visitors, because every tiny detail was perfectly made by hand.","zh":"黃金面具的藝術技巧讓參觀者驚嘆,因為每一個細節都是手工完美製作的。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B79","t":"藝術技巧"},{"w":"ascendancy","pos":"n.","def":"a position of power or control","cn":"優勢;支配地位","s":"The city gained ________ over its neighbours through trade, and soon it controlled the whole coast.","zh":"這座城市透過貿易取得了對鄰近城市的支配地位,很快就控制了整個海岸。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B80","t":"支配地位"},{"w":"calamity","pos":"n.","def":"a sudden event that causes great damage","cn":"災難;大禍","s":"The flood was a terrible ________ for the farming town, and many families lost their homes and animals.","zh":"這場洪水對這個農業小鎮是一場可怕的災難,許多家庭失去了家園和牲畜。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B81","t":"災難"},{"w":"commonality","pos":"n.","def":"a shared feature or interest","cn":"共同點","s":"There is a clear ________ between the two cultures, because both built pyramids and worshipped the sun.","zh":"這兩種文化之間有明顯的共同點,因為兩者都建造金字塔並崇拜太陽。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B82","t":"共同點"},{"w":"connotation","pos":"n.","def":"an extra feeling or idea that a word suggests","cn":"言外之意;含義","s":"The word \"barbarian\" has a negative ________, but in ancient Greek it simply meant someone who spoke another language.","zh":"「野蠻人」這個字帶有負面的含義,但在古希臘語中它只是指說另一種語言的人。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B83","t":"含義"},{"w":"continuity","pos":"n.","def":"the state of continuing without stopping or changing","cn":"連續性;延續","s":"There is great ________ in the village's traditions, because people still celebrate festivals that began a thousand years ago.","zh":"這個村莊的傳統有很強的延續性,因為人們仍然慶祝始於一千年前的節慶。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B84","t":"延續性"},{"w":"cornerstone","pos":"n.","def":"the most important part on which something is based","cn":"基石;基礎","s":"Farming was the ________ of the ancient economy, so a bad harvest could make the whole kingdom poor.","zh":"農業是古代經濟的基石,所以一次歉收就可能讓整個王國陷入貧困。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B85","t":"基石"},{"w":"custodian","pos":"n.","def":"a person or group responsible for protecting something","cn":"守護者;保管人","s":"The museum sees itself as the ________ of the nation's history, so it takes great care of every object.","zh":"博物館把自己視為國家歷史的守護者,所以它非常細心地照顧每一件物品。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B86","t":"守護者"},{"w":"dawn","pos":"n.","def":"the beginning of something","cn":"開端;黎明","s":"The ________ of farming happened about ten thousand years ago, and it slowly changed the way humans lived.","zh":"農業的開端大約在一萬年前,它逐漸改變了人類的生活方式。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B87","t":"開端"},{"w":"decadence","pos":"n.","def":"behaviour showing too much love of pleasure and luxury","cn":"頹廢;墮落","s":"Some writers blamed the ________ of the rich for the fall of Rome, although historians now point to many other causes.","zh":"一些作家把羅馬的衰亡歸咎於富人的頹廢,雖然歷史學家現在指出了許多其他原因。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B88","t":"頹廢"},{"w":"descendant","pos":"n.","def":"a person related to someone who lived long ago","cn":"後裔;子孫","s":"DNA tests showed that the farmer was a ________ of the ancient king, and the news surprised his whole village.","zh":"DNA檢測顯示這位農夫是那位古代國王的後裔,這個消息讓全村都感到驚訝。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B89","t":"後裔"},{"w":"dominion","pos":"n.","def":"the power to rule, or the land that someone rules","cn":"統治權;領土","s":"The king had ________ over a vast area, but he rarely visited the distant parts of his land.","zh":"國王擁有廣大地區的統治權,但他很少造訪領土的偏遠地區。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B90","t":"統治權"},{"w":"edifice","pos":"n.","def":"a large, impressive building","cn":"宏偉建築;大廈","s":"The palace was a magnificent ________ of marble and gold, so visitors from other lands were amazed by it.","zh":"這座宮殿是一座用大理石和黃金建成的宏偉建築,所以來自其他地方的訪客都被它震撼。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B91","t":"宏偉建築"},{"w":"entirety","pos":"n.","def":"the whole of something","cn":"全部;整體","s":"The museum will show the collection in its ________ for the first time, so visitors can see all five hundred objects.","zh":"博物館將首次展出收藏品的全部,所以參觀者可以看到全部五百件物品。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B92","t":"全部"},{"w":"excerpt","pos":"n.","def":"a short part taken from a longer text","cn":"摘錄;節選","s":"Our teacher read an ________ from an ancient diary, and we learned how a Roman soldier felt about his job.","zh":"老師朗讀了一段古代日記的節選,我們了解了一名羅馬士兵對他的工作有什麼感受。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B93","t":"節選"},{"w":"exodus","pos":"n.","def":"a situation where many people leave a place at the same time","cn":"大批離開;出走","s":"There was a mass ________ from the city after the river dried up, so the streets were soon empty.","zh":"河流乾涸後,城市出現了大規模的人口外移,所以街道很快就空了。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B94","t":"人口外移"},{"w":"expanse","pos":"n.","def":"a wide, open area of land, sea or sky","cn":"廣闊的區域","s":"A huge ________ of desert separated the two cities, so traders needed camels to carry water.","zh":"一大片廣闊的沙漠隔開了這兩座城市,所以商人需要駱駝來運水。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B95","t":"廣闊的"},{"w":"fabric","pos":"n.","def":"the basic structure of a society","cn":"結構;構造","s":"Long years of war and disease destroyed the ________ of society, and many villages were never rebuilt.","zh":"多年的戰爭和疾病摧毀了社會的結構,許多村莊再也沒有重建。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B96","t":"結構"},{"w":"faction","pos":"n.","def":"a small group within a larger group, often in conflict","cn":"派系;派別","s":"One ________ in the senate wanted peace, but the other group pushed the city into a long war.","zh":"元老院中的一個派系希望和平,但另一派把城市推向了一場漫長的戰爭。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B97","t":"派系"},{"w":"feud","pos":"n.","def":"a long, bitter argument between families or groups","cn":"世仇;長期爭執","s":"The ________ between the two families lasted for generations, and nobody could remember how it started.","zh":"這兩個家族之間的世仇持續了好幾代,沒有人記得它是怎麼開始的。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B98","t":"世仇"},{"w":"folklore","pos":"n.","def":"traditional stories and beliefs of a community","cn":"民間傳說;民俗","s":"According to local ________, a dragon once lived in the hills, so the villagers built a temple to keep it calm.","zh":"根據當地的民間傳說,山丘上曾經住著一條龍,所以村民們建了一座廟來安撫牠。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B99","t":"民間傳說"},{"w":"forerunner","pos":"n.","def":"something that came before and led to something newer","cn":"先驅;前身","s":"The ancient Chinese compass was a ________ of modern navigation tools, and it helped sailors travel much farther.","zh":"古代中國的指南針是現代導航工具的前身,它幫助水手航行得更遠。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B100","t":"前身"},{"w":"fusion","pos":"n.","def":"a mixture of different things joined together","cn":"融合","s":"The city's art shows a ________ of Greek and Indian styles, because the two cultures met there through trade.","zh":"這座城市的藝術呈現了希臘和印度風格的融合,因為這兩種文化透過貿易在那裡相遇。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B101","t":"融合"},{"w":"genesis","pos":"n.","def":"the beginning or origin of something","cn":"起源;開端","s":"The ________ of the Olympic Games goes back to ancient Greece, where athletes competed to honour the gods.","zh":"奧林匹克運動會的起源可以追溯到古希臘,當時運動員比賽是為了榮耀神明。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B102","t":"起源"},{"w":"grandeur","pos":"n.","def":"the quality of being very large and impressive","cn":"宏偉;壯麗","s":"The ________ of the ancient temple took our breath away, and we spent the whole afternoon exploring it.","zh":"那座古老神廟的宏偉讓我們嘆為觀止,我們花了整個下午探索它。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B103","t":"宏偉"},{"w":"habitation","pos":"n.","def":"the act of living in a place","cn":"居住;住所","s":"There are signs of human ________ in the cave, so people probably lived there for thousands of years.","zh":"洞穴裡有人類居住的跡象,所以人們可能在那裡生活了數千年。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B104","t":"居住"},{"w":"heir","pos":"n.","def":"a person who will receive someone's property or position","cn":"繼承人","s":"The king had no ________, so after his death his cousins fought over the throne for many years.","zh":"國王沒有繼承人,所以他死後他的堂兄弟們為了王位爭鬥了好多年。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B105","t":"繼承人"},{"w":"heyday","pos":"n.","def":"the time when something was most successful","cn":"全盛時期","s":"In its ________, the port had hundreds of ships every day, but now it is a quiet fishing village.","zh":"在它的全盛時期,這個港口每天有數百艘船,但現在它是一個安靜的漁村。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B106","t":"全盛時期"},{"w":"homage","pos":"n.","def":"something done to show great respect","cn":"敬意;致敬","s":"Every year, thousands of people pay ________ to the ancient king by visiting his tomb on his birthday.","zh":"每年都有數千人在古代國王生日那天造訪他的陵墓,向他致敬。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B107","t":"致敬"},{"w":"icon","pos":"n.","def":"a famous person or thing that represents an idea","cn":"象徵;代表性人物或事物","s":"The Great Wall has become an ________ of China, and millions of tourists walk along it every year.","zh":"長城已經成為中國的象徵,每年有數百萬遊客沿著它行走。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B108","t":"象徵"},{"w":"imprint","pos":"n.","def":"a mark or lasting effect left by something","cn":"印記;痕跡","s":"The Romans left a deep ________ on European culture, and many modern languages come from Latin.","zh":"羅馬人在歐洲文化上留下了深刻的印記,許多現代語言源自拉丁語。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B109","t":"印記"},{"w":"incursion","pos":"n.","def":"a sudden attack into another country's land","cn":"入侵;侵襲","s":"The wall was built to stop ________ from the north, but enemy soldiers still found ways to get through.","zh":"這道城牆是為了阻止來自北方的侵襲而建造的,但敵軍仍然找到了穿越的方法。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B110","t":"侵襲"},{"w":"intermediary","pos":"n.","def":"a person who helps two sides communicate or trade","cn":"中間人;仲介","s":"Desert tribes acted as an ________ between East and West, so they became rich by moving goods across the sand.","zh":"沙漠部落充當東西方之間的中間人,所以他們靠著穿越沙漠運送貨物而致富。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B111","t":"中間人"},{"w":"juncture","pos":"n.","def":"a particular point in time, especially an important one","cn":"關頭;時刻","s":"At this ________ in history, the small kingdom had to choose between war and peace, and its choice changed everything.","zh":"在歷史的這個關頭,這個小王國必須在戰爭與和平之間做出選擇,而它的選擇改變了一切。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B112","t":"關頭"},{"w":"lore","pos":"n.","def":"knowledge and stories passed down within a group","cn":"傳統知識;口傳故事","s":"Old sailors shared ________ about the stars, so young crew members learned to find their way at night.","zh":"老水手們分享關於星星的傳統知識,所以年輕船員學會在夜裡辨別方向。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B113","t":"傳統知識"},{"w":"majesty","pos":"n.","def":"impressive beauty and greatness","cn":"雄偉;莊嚴","s":"The ________ of the mountain temple impressed every visitor, especially when the morning sun lit up its golden roof.","zh":"山中神廟的莊嚴讓每位訪客印象深刻,尤其是早晨陽光照亮它金色屋頂的時候。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B114","t":"莊嚴"},{"w":"motif","pos":"n.","def":"a pattern or idea that is repeated in art","cn":"圖案;主題","s":"The lotus flower is a common ________ in Egyptian art, and you can see it on walls, jewellery and pottery.","zh":"蓮花是埃及藝術中常見的圖案,你可以在牆壁、珠寶和陶器上看到它。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B115","t":"圖案"},{"w":"mystique","pos":"n.","def":"a quality of mystery that makes something attractive","cn":"神秘感","s":"The lost city has a special ________, so many films and novels have been written about it.","zh":"這座失落之城有一種特殊的神秘感,所以許多電影和小說都以它為題材。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B116","t":"神秘感"},{"w":"patron","pos":"n.","def":"a person who gives money to support artists or projects","cn":"資助者;贊助人","s":"A rich ________ paid for the temple's paintings, and his face was painted among the gods as a reward.","zh":"一位富有的贊助人出資繪製神廟的壁畫,作為回報,他的臉被畫在眾神之中。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B117","t":"贊助人"},{"w":"peril","pos":"n.","def":"great danger","cn":"危險;險境","s":"Sailors faced great ________ on long voyages, because storms and pirates could appear at any time.","zh":"水手們在長途航行中面臨極大的危險,因為暴風雨和海盜隨時可能出現。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B118","t":"危險"},{"w":"posterity","pos":"n.","def":"all the people who will live in the future","cn":"後代;後世","s":"The king built huge monuments for ________, because he wanted people to remember him forever.","zh":"國王為後世建造了巨大的紀念碑,因為他希望人們永遠記住他。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B119","t":"後世"},{"w":"precursor","pos":"n.","def":"something that comes before and leads to something else","cn":"先驅;前兆","s":"The abacus was a ________ of the calculator, and traders used it for thousands of years.","zh":"算盤是計算機的先驅,商人們使用它長達數千年。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B120","t":"先驅"},{"w":"provenance","pos":"n.","def":"the place where something comes from and its history","cn":"出處;來源","s":"The museum checks the ________ of every object, so it does not buy anything that was stolen from a site.","zh":"博物館會查核每件物品的來源,所以它不會購買任何從遺址被盜出的東西。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B121","t":"來源"},{"w":"quest","pos":"n.","def":"a long search for something","cn":"探索;追尋","s":"The explorer's ________ for the lost city lasted twenty years, but he never found what he was looking for.","zh":"這位探險家對失落之城的追尋持續了二十年,但他始終沒有找到他要找的東西。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B122","t":"追尋"},{"w":"refuge","pos":"n.","def":"a place that gives protection from danger","cn":"避難所;庇護","s":"The cave offered ________ during the war, and families hid there until the soldiers left the valley.","zh":"戰爭期間洞穴提供了庇護,家家戶戶躲在那裡直到士兵離開山谷。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B123","t":"庇護"},{"w":"remnant","pos":"n.","def":"a small part that remains of something larger","cn":"殘餘;遺跡","s":"Only a ________ of the old city wall survives today, but it shows how strong the defences once were.","zh":"今天只剩下舊城牆的一小段殘餘,但它顯示了當年的防禦有多堅固。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B124","t":"殘餘"},{"w":"renaissance","pos":"n.","def":"a new period of interest and activity in something","cn":"復興","s":"The town is enjoying a cultural ________, because young artists have opened studios in its old buildings.","zh":"這個城鎮正經歷一場文化復興,因為年輕藝術家在它的老建築裡開設了工作室。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B125","t":"復興"},{"w":"repository","pos":"n.","def":"a place where things are stored","cn":"儲藏處;寶庫","s":"The ancient library was a ________ of knowledge, but a terrible fire destroyed most of its scrolls.","zh":"那座古代圖書館是知識的寶庫,但一場可怕的大火燒毀了它大部分的卷軸。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B126","t":"寶庫"},{"w":"rite","pos":"n.","def":"a traditional ceremony","cn":"儀式;典禮","s":"The ________ of passage marked the day a boy became a man, and the whole village came to watch.","zh":"這個成年儀式標誌著男孩成為男人的那一天,全村的人都來觀禮。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B127","t":"儀式"},{"w":"sanctity","pos":"n.","def":"the quality of being holy or very important","cn":"神聖性","s":"Visitors must respect the ________ of the temple, so they are asked to remove their shoes and speak quietly.","zh":"參觀者必須尊重神廟的神聖性,所以他們被要求脫鞋並輕聲說話。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B128","t":"神聖性"},{"w":"sovereignty","pos":"n.","def":"complete power to govern a country","cn":"主權","s":"The small island fought for its ________ for many years, and finally it became an independent nation.","zh":"這座小島為了它的主權奮鬥了許多年,最後成為一個獨立的國家。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B129","t":"主權"},{"w":"splendour","pos":"n.","def":"great beauty and impressive appearance","cn":"壯麗;輝煌","s":"The ________ of the royal palace showed the power of the king, and foreign visitors were often speechless.","zh":"皇宮的輝煌展現了國王的權勢,外國訪客常常說不出話來。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B130","t":"輝煌"},{"w":"stature","pos":"n.","def":"the importance or reputation of someone","cn":"聲望;地位","s":"The city grew in ________ as more traders arrived, and soon it was the richest place in the region.","zh":"隨著越來越多商人到來,這座城市的地位日漸提高,很快就成為該地區最富裕的地方。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B131","t":"地位"},{"w":"subsistence","pos":"n.","def":"the ability to survive with just enough food","cn":"勉強維生;生存","s":"Most families lived at a ________ level, so they grew only enough food to feed themselves.","zh":"大多數家庭過著勉強維生的生活,所以他們只種植足夠養活自己的食物。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B132","t":"勉強維生"},{"w":"supremacy","pos":"n.","def":"the position of being the most powerful","cn":"霸權;至高無上","s":"The two cities fought for ________ at sea, because the winner would control the rich trade routes.","zh":"這兩座城市為了海上霸權而戰,因為勝利者將控制富饒的貿易路線。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B133","t":"霸權"},{"w":"tenure","pos":"n.","def":"the period when someone holds an important position","cn":"任期;在職期間","s":"During his ________ as governor, he built schools and roads, so people remembered him as a fair leader.","zh":"在他擔任總督的任期內,他興建了學校和道路,所以人們記得他是一位公正的領袖。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B134","t":"任期"},{"w":"testament","pos":"n.","def":"something that clearly shows that something is true","cn":"證明;證據","s":"The pyramids are a ________ to the skill of ancient engineers, because they are still standing after 4,500 years.","zh":"金字塔是古代工程師技術的證明,因為它們在四千五百年後仍然屹立。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B135","t":"證明"},{"w":"turmoil","pos":"n.","def":"a state of great confusion or disorder","cn":"混亂;動盪","s":"The kingdom was in ________ after the king's death, so many people fled to safer lands.","zh":"國王死後王國陷入動盪,所以許多人逃往較安全的地方。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B136","t":"動盪"},{"w":"uprising","pos":"n.","def":"a situation where people fight against those in power","cn":"起義;暴動","s":"The ________ began in the countryside, but it soon spread to the capital and frightened the emperor.","zh":"這場起義從鄉間開始,但很快就蔓延到首都,讓皇帝感到恐慌。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B137","t":"起義"},{"w":"vestige","pos":"n.","def":"a small part or sign of something that once existed","cn":"遺跡;殘跡","s":"The last ________ of the old road can still be seen in the forest, so hikers sometimes walk along it.","zh":"舊道路的最後遺跡仍然可以在森林中看到,所以登山客有時會沿著它行走。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B138","t":"遺跡"},{"w":"zenith","pos":"n.","def":"the time when something is most powerful or successful","cn":"頂峰;鼎盛時期","s":"At its ________, the empire controlled most of the known world, and its capital had a million people.","zh":"在它的鼎盛時期,這個帝國控制了大部分已知世界,首都有一百萬人口。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B139","t":"鼎盛時期"},{"w":"agrarian","pos":"adj.","def":"connected with farming and farmland","cn":"農業的;土地的","s":"Most ancient societies were ________, so the success of the harvest decided whether people lived or starved.","zh":"大多數古代社會都是農業社會,所以收成好壞決定了人們是溫飽還是挨餓。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B140","t":"農業"},{"w":"arcane","pos":"adj.","def":"secret and understood by only a few people","cn":"神秘的;深奧難懂的","s":"The priests used ________ symbols that ordinary people could not read, so their power seemed almost magical.","zh":"祭司們使用一般人看不懂的神秘符號,所以他們的力量看起來幾乎像魔法。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B141","t":"神秘"},{"w":"barren","pos":"adj.","def":"too dry or poor for plants to grow","cn":"貧瘠的;荒蕪的","s":"The land around the ruins is now ________, but pollen studies show that it was once covered in forests.","zh":"遺址周圍的土地現在很貧瘠,但花粉研究顯示那裡曾經被森林覆蓋。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B142","t":"貧瘠"},{"w":"bygone","pos":"adj.","def":"belonging to a time in the past","cn":"過去的;往昔的","s":"The old photographs remind us of a ________ age, when people travelled by horse and wrote letters by hand.","zh":"這些老照片讓我們想起往昔的時代,那時人們騎馬旅行並用手寫信。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B143","t":"往昔的"},{"w":"ceremonial","pos":"adj.","def":"used in or connected with a formal ceremony","cn":"儀式的;禮儀上的","s":"The golden knife was probably ________, because it was too soft to cut anything and it showed no signs of use.","zh":"這把黃金刀可能是儀式用的,因為它太軟無法切任何東西,而且沒有使用過的痕跡。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B144","t":"儀式用的"},{"w":"classical","pos":"adj.","def":"connected with ancient Greece and Rome","cn":"古典的;古希臘羅馬的","s":"Many government buildings copy ________ designs, so they have tall white columns like Greek temples.","zh":"許多政府建築模仿古典設計,所以它們有像希臘神廟一樣高大的白色柱子。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B145","t":"古典"},{"w":"colossal","pos":"adj.","def":"extremely large","cn":"巨大的;龐大的","s":"A ________ statue of the king once stood at the harbour entrance, and ships sailed between its legs.","zh":"一座國王的巨大雕像曾經矗立在港口入口,船隻從它的雙腿之間駛過。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B146","t":"巨大"},{"w":"communal","pos":"adj.","def":"shared by everyone in a group","cn":"公共的;共用的","s":"The village had a ________ oven, so families took turns baking their bread there every morning.","zh":"村莊有一座共用的烤爐,所以各家每天早上輪流在那裡烤麵包。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B147","t":"共用的"},{"w":"cryptic","pos":"adj.","def":"having a hidden meaning that is hard to understand","cn":"晦澀的;隱晦的","s":"The message carved on the stone was ________, and scholars still argue about what it means.","zh":"刻在石頭上的訊息很隱晦,學者們至今仍在爭論它的意思。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B148","t":"隱晦"},{"w":"defunct","pos":"adj.","def":"no longer existing or working","cn":"已不存在的;已廢棄的","s":"The old railway is now ________, but the station has been turned into a small history museum.","zh":"那條舊鐵路現在已經廢棄,但車站已被改建成一座小型歷史博物館。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B149","t":"廢棄"},{"w":"dilapidated","pos":"adj.","def":"old and in very bad condition","cn":"破舊的;年久失修的","s":"The ________ castle was almost falling down, so the town raised money to repair its towers.","zh":"那座年久失修的城堡幾乎要倒塌了,所以小鎮募款修復它的塔樓。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B150","t":"年久失修的"},{"w":"exquisite","pos":"adj.","def":"extremely beautiful and delicate","cn":"精緻的;精美的","s":"The museum displays an ________ gold necklace, and its tiny flowers are smaller than a grain of rice.","zh":"博物館展示了一條精緻的金項鍊,上面的小花比一粒米還小。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B151","t":"精緻的"},{"w":"extant","pos":"adj.","def":"still existing, especially from long ago","cn":"現存的","s":"Only three copies of the ancient book are ________, so each one is extremely valuable.","zh":"這本古書只有三本現存,所以每一本都極為珍貴。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B152","t":"現存"},{"w":"fabled","pos":"adj.","def":"famous and talked about in old stories","cn":"傳說中的;著名的","s":"Explorers searched for the ________ city of gold, but most of them returned with nothing.","zh":"探險家們尋找傳說中的黃金之城,但大多數人空手而歸。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B153","t":"傳說中的"},{"w":"fertile","pos":"adj.","def":"able to produce good crops","cn":"肥沃的","s":"The river flooded every year and left ________ soil behind, so farmers could grow plenty of wheat.","zh":"河流每年氾濫並留下肥沃的土壤,所以農民能種出大量的小麥。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B154","t":"肥沃的"},{"w":"feudal","pos":"adj.","def":"connected with a system where peasants worked land for lords","cn":"封建的","s":"In the ________ system, peasants worked on the lord's land, and in return he protected them from enemies.","zh":"在封建制度下,農民在領主的土地上工作,作為回報,領主保護他們免受敵人侵擾。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B155","t":"封建"},{"w":"geographical","pos":"adj.","def":"connected with the natural features of an area","cn":"地理的","s":"The city's ________ position between two seas made it rich, because every trader had to pass through it.","zh":"這座城市位於兩海之間的地理位置讓它變得富裕,因為每個商人都必須經過那裡。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B156","t":"地理"},{"w":"hereditary","pos":"adj.","def":"passed from parents to children","cn":"世襲的;遺傳的","s":"The title of king was ________, so the oldest son usually became the next ruler.","zh":"國王的頭銜是世襲的,所以通常由長子成為下一任統治者。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B157","t":"世襲的"},{"w":"historic","pos":"adj.","def":"important in history","cn":"有歷史意義的","s":"The ________ agreement ended a war that had lasted fifty years, and both sides celebrated for a week.","zh":"這份具有歷史意義的協議結束了一場持續了五十年的戰爭,雙方慶祝了一個星期。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B158","t":"具有歷史意義的"},{"w":"imperial","pos":"adj.","def":"connected with an empire or an emperor","cn":"帝國的;皇帝的","s":"The ________ palace had walls painted red, and ordinary people were not allowed to enter it.","zh":"皇宮的牆漆成紅色,一般百姓不被允許進入。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B159","t":"皇"},{"w":"inhospitable","pos":"adj.","def":"difficult to live in because of harsh conditions","cn":"不適合居住的;荒涼的","s":"The desert is an ________ place, but ancient traders crossed it regularly with camels and water bags.","zh":"沙漠是一個不適合居住的地方,但古代商人經常帶著駱駝和水袋穿越它。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B160","t":"不適合居住的"},{"w":"lavish","pos":"adj.","def":"very generous, rich or expensive","cn":"奢華的;大量的","s":"The king held ________ parties in his palace, while many of his people did not have enough to eat.","zh":"國王在宮殿裡舉辦奢華的宴會,而他的許多人民卻吃不飽。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B161","t":"奢華的"},{"w":"makeshift","pos":"adj.","def":"made quickly to be used for a short time","cn":"臨時的;權宜的","s":"After the flood, families lived in ________ shelters made of branches, so the winter was very hard for them.","zh":"洪水過後,家家戶戶住在用樹枝搭成的臨時棚屋裡,所以那個冬天對他們來說非常艱難。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B162","t":"臨時"},{"w":"medieval","pos":"adj.","def":"from the Middle Ages, about 500 to 1500 AD","cn":"中世紀的","s":"The ________ town still has narrow streets and stone walls, so walking there feels like travelling back in time.","zh":"這座中世紀小鎮仍然保有狹窄的街道和石牆,所以走在那裡感覺就像回到過去。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B163","t":"中世紀"},{"w":"opulent","pos":"adj.","def":"showing great wealth; very luxurious","cn":"富麗堂皇的;豪華的","s":"The ________ rooms of the palace were full of gold and silk, and each one was decorated differently.","zh":"宮殿中富麗堂皇的房間裡堆滿了黃金和絲綢,每一間的裝飾都不一樣。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B164","t":"富麗堂皇的"},{"w":"ornate","pos":"adj.","def":"decorated with many complicated details","cn":"裝飾華麗的","s":"The church has an ________ ceiling covered with paintings, so visitors often lie on the benches to look up at it.","zh":"這座教堂有一片繪滿壁畫的華麗天花板,所以參觀者常常躺在長椅上仰望它。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B165","t":"華麗"},{"w":"pastoral","pos":"adj.","def":"connected with country life and keeping animals","cn":"田園的;畜牧的","s":"The ________ people moved their sheep between the mountains and valleys, following the grass each season.","zh":"這些畜牧民族在山區和山谷之間遷移他們的羊群,每個季節跟著青草走。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B166","t":"畜牧"},{"w":"rugged","pos":"adj.","def":"rough, rocky and difficult to travel across","cn":"崎嶇的;多岩石的","s":"The ________ mountains protected the kingdom from invaders, because armies could not march through them easily.","zh":"崎嶇的山脈保護王國免受入侵,因為軍隊無法輕易地穿越。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B167","t":"崎嶇的"},{"w":"sacred","pos":"adj.","def":"holy and connected with a god","cn":"神聖的","s":"The mountain was ________ to the local people, so nobody was allowed to climb to the top.","zh":"那座山對當地人來說是神聖的,所以沒有人被允許爬到山頂。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B168","t":"神聖的"},{"w":"secular","pos":"adj.","def":"not connected with religion","cn":"世俗的;非宗教的","s":"Most ancient buildings were temples, but this ________ building was used for markets and meetings.","zh":"大多數古代建築是神廟,但這棟世俗的建築被用作市集和集會場所。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B169","t":"世俗的"},{"w":"sprawling","pos":"adj.","def":"spreading out over a large area","cn":"延伸廣闊的;雜亂擴展的","s":"The ________ ancient city covered more than twenty square kilometres, and only a small part has been excavated.","zh":"這座廣闊延伸的古城占地超過二十平方公里,只有一小部分被發掘過。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B170","t":"廣闊延伸的"},{"w":"subterranean","pos":"adj.","def":"existing under the ground","cn":"地下的","s":"The city had a ________ network of tunnels, so people could hide underground when enemies attacked.","zh":"這座城市有一個地下隧道網絡,所以敵人來襲時人們可以躲到地下。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B171","t":"地下"},{"w":"weathered","pos":"adj.","def":"changed in colour or shape by wind and rain","cn":"風化的;飽經風霜的","s":"The ________ statues have lost their noses and fingers, but you can still see the shape of their faces.","zh":"那些風化的雕像已經失去了鼻子和手指,但你仍然可以看出它們臉部的輪廓。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B172","t":"風化的"},{"w":"indelible","pos":"adj.","def":"impossible to remove or forget","cn":"不可磨滅的;難忘的","s":"The Roman Empire left an ________ mark on Europe, and we can still see it in roads, laws and languages.","zh":"羅馬帝國在歐洲留下了不可磨滅的印記,我們至今仍能在道路、法律和語言中看到它。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B173","t":"不可磨滅的"},{"w":"perennial","pos":"adj.","def":"lasting for a very long time or happening again and again","cn":"長期的;反覆出現的","s":"Water shortage was a ________ problem in the desert city, so engineers built huge underground tanks.","zh":"缺水是這座沙漠城市長期存在的問題,所以工程師建造了巨大的地下水槽。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B174","t":"長期存在的"},{"w":"renowned","pos":"adj.","def":"famous and respected","cn":"著名的;享有盛譽的","s":"The city was ________ for its glassmaking, and its beautiful cups were sold as far away as China.","zh":"這座城市以玻璃製造聞名,它美麗的杯子遠銷到中國。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B175","t":"聞名"},{"w":"self-sufficient","pos":"adj.","def":"able to provide everything you need without help","cn":"自給自足的","s":"The monastery was ________, because the monks grew their own food and made their own clothes.","zh":"這座修道院是自給自足的,因為修士們自己種植食物並製作衣服。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B176","t":"自給自足的"},{"w":"staple","pos":"adj.","def":"most important or most commonly used","cn":"主要的;基本的","s":"Rice was the ________ food in the region, so a poor harvest meant hunger for almost everyone.","zh":"米是這個地區的主要食物,所以歉收意味著幾乎每個人都會挨餓。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B177","t":"主要"},{"w":"strategic","pos":"adj.","def":"important for achieving a military or political aim","cn":"戰略的;戰略上重要的","s":"The fortress was built in a ________ position above the river, so soldiers could watch every boat that passed.","zh":"這座堡壘建在河流上方一個戰略位置,所以士兵能監視每一艘經過的船。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B178","t":"戰略"},{"w":"sumptuous","pos":"adj.","def":"very expensive and impressive","cn":"奢華的;豐盛的","s":"The king served a ________ meal to his guests, and it included roast peacock and rare fruits.","zh":"國王為客人準備了一頓豐盛的大餐,包括烤孔雀和珍稀水果。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B179","t":"豐盛的"},{"w":"vibrant","pos":"adj.","def":"full of energy and life","cn":"充滿活力的;鮮豔的","s":"The ancient market was a ________ place, where traders from many lands shouted prices in different languages.","zh":"古代市集是一個充滿活力的地方,來自各地的商人用不同的語言喊價。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B180","t":"充滿活力的"},{"w":"desolate","pos":"adj.","def":"empty and without people, often sad","cn":"荒涼的;無人煙的","s":"The once busy city is now ________, and only the wind moves through its empty streets.","zh":"這座曾經熱鬧的城市現在一片荒涼,只有風吹過它空蕩的街道。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B181","t":"荒涼"},{"w":"humble","pos":"adj.","def":"simple and not rich or important","cn":"簡陋的;卑微的","s":"The great emperor came from a ________ family of farmers, but he rose to power through his skill in battle.","zh":"這位偉大的皇帝出身於一個卑微的農民家庭,但他靠著戰鬥才能崛起掌權。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B182","t":"卑微的"},{"w":"stately","pos":"adj.","def":"impressive and grand in appearance","cn":"莊嚴的;宏偉的","s":"The ________ old house stands in a large park, and its rooms are filled with paintings and old furniture.","zh":"那棟宏偉的老宅矗立在一座大公園裡,房間裡擺滿了畫作和古老的家具。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B183","t":"宏偉的"},{"w":"timeless","pos":"adj.","def":"not affected by changes in time or fashion","cn":"永恆的;不受時間影響的","s":"The ________ beauty of Greek statues still inspires artists, although they were made over two thousand years ago.","zh":"希臘雕像永恆的美至今仍啟發著藝術家,雖然它們是兩千多年前製作的。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B184","t":"永恆的"},{"w":"lasting","pos":"adj.","def":"continuing for a long time","cn":"持久的;長久的","s":"The invention of paper had a ________ effect on the world, because books became cheaper and easier to make.","zh":"紙的發明對世界產生了持久的影響,因為書變得更便宜也更容易製作。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B185","t":"持久的"},{"w":"formerly","pos":"adv.","def":"in the past; before now","cn":"以前;從前","s":"The library was ________ a royal palace, but now anyone can walk in and read the books for free.","zh":"這座圖書館以前是皇宮,但現在任何人都可以走進去免費看書。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B186","t":"以前"},{"w":"reputedly","pos":"adv.","def":"according to what people say","cn":"據說;據稱","s":"The castle is ________ haunted by a queen, so many visitors come at night hoping to see her ghost.","zh":"據說這座城堡有一位女王的鬼魂出沒,所以許多遊客晚上來希望看到她。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B187","t":"據說"},{"w":"supposedly","pos":"adv.","def":"according to what is generally believed, although it may not be true","cn":"據稱;按理說","s":"The sword ________ belonged to a famous king, but tests showed that it was made much later.","zh":"這把劍據稱屬於一位著名的國王,但檢測顯示它是很久以後才製造的。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B188","t":"據稱"},{"w":"meanwhile","pos":"adv.","def":"at the same time; while something else is happening","cn":"同時;與此同時","s":"The men went hunting in the forest, and ________ the women gathered fruit and looked after the children.","zh":"男人們到森林裡打獵,與此同時,女人們採集水果並照顧孩子。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B189","t":"與此同時"},{"w":"chiefly","pos":"adv.","def":"mainly; mostly","cn":"主要地","s":"The city became rich ________ through the salt trade, because salt was needed to keep food fresh.","zh":"這座城市主要透過鹽的貿易而致富,因為人們需要鹽來保存食物。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B190","t":"主要"},{"w":"remarkably","pos":"adv.","def":"in a surprising way","cn":"驚人地;非常","s":"The ancient boat was ________ well preserved, so experts could see the marks made by the builders' tools.","zh":"這艘古船保存得非常好,所以專家能看到造船工人工具留下的痕跡。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B191","t":"非常"},{"w":"astonishingly","pos":"adv.","def":"in a very surprising way","cn":"令人驚訝地","s":"________, the seeds found in the tomb started to grow when scientists planted them, although they were two thousand years old.","zh":"令人驚訝的是,科學家種下在墳墓中發現的種子後它們竟然開始發芽,雖然它們已有兩千年的歷史。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B192","t":"令人驚訝的是"},{"w":"densely","pos":"adv.","def":"with many people or things close together","cn":"密集地;稠密地","s":"The ancient city was ________ populated, so houses were built right next to each other with no gardens.","zh":"這座古城人口稠密,所以房子緊挨著建造,沒有花園。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B193","t":"稠密"},{"w":"painstakingly","pos":"adv.","def":"very carefully and with great effort","cn":"煞費苦心地;仔細地","s":"The team ________ glued thousands of pottery pieces back together, and the work took more than two years.","zh":"團隊煞費苦心地把數千片陶器碎片重新黏合起來,這項工作花了兩年多。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B194","t":"煞費苦心地"},{"w":"barely","pos":"adv.","def":"only just; almost not","cn":"勉強;幾乎不","s":"The writing on the stone is ________ visible today, so experts use special lights to read it.","zh":"石頭上的文字如今幾乎看不見了,所以專家使用特殊燈光來閱讀。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B195","t":"幾乎 不"},{"w":"presently","pos":"adv.","def":"at the present time; now","cn":"目前;現在","s":"The statue is ________ in a museum in London, but many people believe it should return to Greece.","zh":"這座雕像目前在倫敦的一間博物館裡,但許多人認為它應該歸還給希臘。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B196","t":"目前"},{"w":"duly","pos":"adv.","def":"in the correct or expected way","cn":"適當地;如期地","s":"The ancient tax was ________ paid by every family, and scribes recorded each payment on clay tablets.","zh":"古代的稅如期由每個家庭繳納,書記們把每一筆款項記錄在泥板上。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B197","t":"如期"},{"w":"wholly","pos":"adv.","def":"completely; fully","cn":"完全地;全部","s":"The temple was ________ built by hand, so it took thousands of workers many years to finish it.","zh":"這座神廟完全是手工建造的,所以數千名工人花了許多年才完成。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B198","t":"完全"},{"w":"inextricably","pos":"adv.","def":"in a way that cannot be separated","cn":"密不可分地","s":"The history of the city is ________ linked to the river, because the river brought water, food and trade.","zh":"這座城市的歷史與河流密不可分,因為河流帶來了水、食物和貿易。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B199","t":"密不可分"},{"w":"irretrievably","pos":"adv.","def":"in a way that cannot be got back or repaired","cn":"無法挽回地","s":"Many ancient books were ________ lost in the fire, so we will never know what they said.","zh":"許多古書在大火中無法挽回地遺失了,所以我們永遠不會知道它們寫了什麼。","part":"B","sec":"Part B 學術單字","lab":"B200","t":"無法挽回地"},{"w":"date back to","pos":"v.phr.","def":"to have existed since a particular time in the past","cn":"追溯到;始於","s":"The oldest part of the castle seems to ______ ______ ______ the twelfth century, but the towers were added much later.","zh":"這座城堡最古老的部分似乎可追溯到十二世紀,但塔樓是很久以後才加上去的。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P1","t":"可追溯到"},{"w":"set in stone","pos":"adj.phr.","def":"fixed and impossible to change","cn":"一成不變的;不可更改的","s":"Our plans for the museum trip are not ______ ______ ______, so we can change the date if it rains.","zh":"我們參觀博物館的計畫並不是一成不變的,所以如果下雨我們可以改日期。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P2","t":"一成不變的"},{"w":"leave no stone unturned","pos":"v.phr.","def":"to try every possible way to find something","cn":"千方百計;不遺餘力","s":"The archaeologists promised to ______ ______ ______ ______ in their search for the lost tomb, so they checked every hill in the valley.","zh":"考古學家承諾在尋找失落墳墓時會不遺餘力,所以他們檢查了山谷中的每一座山丘。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P3","t":"不遺餘力"},{"w":"a stone's throw","pos":"n.phr.","def":"a very short distance","cn":"一箭之遙;很近的距離","s":"Our hotel was just ______ ______ ______ from the ancient amphitheatre, so we walked there every evening.","zh":"我們的飯店離古代圓形劇場只有一箭之遙,所以我們每天晚上都走路過去。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P4","t":"一箭之遙"},{"w":"piece together","pos":"v.phr.","def":"to understand a situation by putting separate facts together","cn":"拼湊出;理清","s":"Historians used letters and coins to ______ ______ the story of the city, although many records were lost.","zh":"歷史學家利用信件和錢幣拼湊出這座城市的故事,雖然許多紀錄已經遺失。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P5","t":"拼湊出"},{"w":"come to light","pos":"v.phr.","def":"to become known","cn":"被發現;暴露出來","s":"New facts about the ancient king ______ ______ ______ last year, when workers found his letters in a library basement.","zh":"關於這位古代國王的新事實在去年被發現,當時工人在圖書館地下室找到了他的信件。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P6","t":"被發現"},{"w":"stand the test of time","pos":"v.phr.","def":"to stay strong or popular for a very long time","cn":"經得起時間的考驗","s":"Roman roads have ______ ______ ______ ______ ______, and some of them are still used by cars today.","zh":"羅馬道路經得起時間的考驗,其中一些至今仍有汽車行駛。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P7","t":"經得起時間的考驗"},{"w":"lay the foundations for","pos":"v.phr.","def":"to create the basic conditions for something to develop","cn":"為…奠定基礎","s":"Greek thinkers helped ______ ______ ______ ______ modern science, because they tried to explain nature through reason.","zh":"希臘思想家幫助為現代科學奠定基礎,因為他們試圖用理性解釋自然。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P8","t":"為 奠定基礎"},{"w":"rise and fall","pos":"n.phr.","def":"the growth and later decline of something","cn":"興衰;盛衰","s":"The book describes the ______ ______ ______ of the Roman Empire, and it explains why such a powerful state collapsed.","zh":"這本書描述了羅馬帝國的興衰,並解釋了為什麼這麼強大的國家會崩潰。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P9","t":"興衰"},{"w":"the cradle of civilisation","pos":"n.phr.","def":"the place where an early civilisation first developed","cn":"文明的搖籃","s":"Mesopotamia is often called ______ ______ ______ ______, because the first cities and writing appeared there.","zh":"美索不達米亞常被稱為文明的搖籃,因為最早的城市和文字出現在那裡。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P10","t":"文明的搖籃"},{"w":"go down in history","pos":"v.phr.","def":"to be remembered for a long time because of something important","cn":"載入史冊;名留青史","s":"The discovery of the young king's tomb will ______ ______ ______ ______ as one of the greatest finds ever.","zh":"這位年輕國王陵墓的發現將作為有史以來最偉大的發現之一而載入史冊。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P11","t":"載入史冊"},{"w":"pass down","pos":"v.phr.","def":"to give knowledge or objects to younger generations","cn":"傳承;流傳下來","s":"Families used to ______ ______ old stories from parents to children, because most people could not read or write.","zh":"家族過去會把古老的故事從父母傳給孩子,因為大多數人不會讀寫。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P12","t":"傳"},{"w":"time will tell","pos":"phr.","def":"the truth will become clear in the future","cn":"時間會證明一切","s":"Nobody knows if the new theory about the pyramids is correct, but ______ ______ ______ as more evidence is found.","zh":"沒有人知道關於金字塔的新理論是否正確,但隨著更多證據被發現,時間會證明一切。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P13","t":"時間會證明一切"},{"w":"turn back the clock","pos":"v.phr.","def":"to return to an earlier time or situation","cn":"讓時光倒流;回到過去","s":"Visiting the old village feels like a way to ______ ______ ______ ______, because people still farm without machines there.","zh":"參觀這個古老村莊感覺像是讓時光倒流,因為那裡的人們仍然不用機器耕種。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P14","t":"讓時光倒流"},{"w":"Rome wasn't built in a day","pos":"phr.","def":"important things take a long time to achieve","cn":"羅馬不是一天造成的","s":"Learning to read ancient languages is slow, but ______ ______ ______ ______ ______ ______, so keep practising every day.","zh":"學習閱讀古代語言很慢,但羅馬不是一天造成的,所以每天持續練習吧。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P15","t":"羅馬不是一天造成的"},{"w":"all roads lead to Rome","pos":"phr.","def":"there are many ways to reach the same goal","cn":"條條大路通羅馬","s":"You can study history at university or in a museum job, because ______ ______ ______ ______ ______ if you are passionate.","zh":"你可以在大學或博物館工作中學習歷史,因為只要你有熱情,條條大路通羅馬。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P16","t":"條條大路通羅馬"},{"w":"hidden in plain sight","pos":"adj.phr.","def":"easy to see but not noticed","cn":"藏在顯眼處;近在眼前卻未被注意","s":"The ancient carving was ______ ______ ______ ______ on the church wall, but nobody noticed it until a student took a photo.","zh":"那幅古代雕刻就近在眼前地刻在教堂牆上,但直到一名學生拍了照片才有人注意到。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P17","t":"近在眼前"},{"w":"scratch the surface","pos":"v.phr.","def":"to deal with only a small part of a subject","cn":"只觸及皮毛","s":"After ten years of digging, the team has only ______ ______ ______ of the huge ancient city, so there is much more to find.","zh":"經過十年的挖掘,團隊對這座巨大的古城只觸及皮毛,所以還有更多東西等待發現。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P18","t":"觸及皮毛"},{"w":"bury the hatchet","pos":"v.phr.","def":"to stop arguing and become friends again","cn":"言歸於好;握手言和","s":"The two kings finally decided to ______ ______ ______, and they signed a peace treaty after years of war.","zh":"兩位國王終於決定握手言和,他們在多年戰爭之後簽署了和平條約。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P19","t":"握手言和"},{"w":"lost in the mists of time","pos":"adj.phr.","def":"forgotten because it happened very long ago","cn":"湮沒在歷史長河中","s":"The name of the person who built the stone circle is ______ ______ ______ ______ ______ ______, so we may never know it.","zh":"建造這個石圈的人的名字已經湮沒在歷史長河中,所以我們可能永遠無法知道。","part":"C","sec":"Part C 固定片語","lab":"P20","t":"湮沒在歷史長河中"}]};
